window.GEAR_BOOK_CONTENTS["book-41"] = [{"id":1,"rawContent":"# 第五章：被判定「自殺」的豪門鋼琴師\n\n週二下午三點十五分。新北市新店區，青山別墅特區。\n\n這是一座依山傍水、門禁森嚴的頂級隱密社區。秋日的陽光透過茂密的落羽松林灑落下來，在寬闊整潔的柏油路面上留下斑駁樹影。\n\n然而，在一棟白色現代極簡風格的三層半獨棟豪宅前，刺眼的黃色警用封鎖線正隨風劇烈晃動著。\n\n豪宅下方的花崗岩景觀庭院裡，一灘暗紅色的刺目血泊已經凝固，幾朵被壓爛的白玫瑰花瓣浸泡在血泊邊緣。\n\n法醫<u>陳念舟</u>提著沉重的不鏽鋼外勤勘驗箱，踩著台階走上三樓半的天台。\n\n這座天台被改造成了一間視野極佳的環景玻璃琴房。琴房的正中央擺放著一台價值數百萬的史坦威三角鋼琴，黑白琴鍵在陽光下泛著冰冷而優雅的象牙光澤。\n\n琴房推拉門大開，外側的鋼化玻璃護欄高度約一米二。此時，地檢署承辦檢察官與刑警大隊偵查佐<u>許書晴</u>正站在護欄旁勘驗現場。\n\n「現場初步狀況很清楚。」\n\n承辦檢察官推了推無框眼鏡，低頭看著筆記本上的紀錄：\n\n「死者沈語萱，二十六歲，國內知名青年鋼琴家。今天上午十一點左右，被前來打掃的鐘點傭人發現墜落在一樓庭院。琴房的茶几上放著三瓶抗憂鬱藥物百憂解、半瓶沒喝完的紅酒，地面上有大量撕碎的樂譜殘頁。垃圾桶裡還找到了一張手寫便條，寫著：『我彈不出妳要的聲音了，這雙手好累。』」\n\n檢察官轉頭看向站在外側、一名穿著名貴黑色定制西裝、眼眶泛紅的年輕男子：\n\n「趙先生，您最後一次見到沈小姐是什麼時候？」\n\n年輕男子掏出雪白的亞麻手帕，擦了擦眼角並不存在的淚水，聲音哽咽得恰到好處：\n\n「昨晚……昨晚十點多。她是個完美的藝術家，自我要求極高。下個月就是她在國家音樂廳的個人獨奏會，她這半年來每天練琴超過十二個小時，常常焦慮到整夜失眠……昨晚她情緒失控跟我大吵了一架，我為了讓她冷靜，就先回市區的公寓了……沒想到……沒想到她竟然會想不開……」\n\n男子死死攥著手帕，身軀微微顫抖，一副痛失愛侶、悲痛欲絕的深情模樣：\n\n「檢察官，語萱生前最愛乾淨，也最注重體面……如果相驗確定是墜樓自殺，請務必盡快發還遺體，我想讓她體體面面地入土為安，不要再讓她受解剖之苦了……」\n\n「趙先生放心，我們會依法處理。」檢察官點了點頭。\n\n<u>許書晴</u>抱著公文夾站在一旁，眉頭卻緊緊鎖在一起。她的直覺告訴她哪裡有些說不出的違和感，但現場無論是門窗反鎖的痕跡、未喝完的酒杯，還是那張筆跡吻合的便條，所有的表象都指向一場典型因憂鬱症失控引發的墜樓輕生。\n\n這時，<u>念舟</u>戴著白手套走了過來。\n\n他蹲在護欄旁，仔細看著玻璃邊緣的擦拭痕跡，又低頭看了一眼地面上那些被撕成碎片的樂譜。\n\n<u>念舟</u>伸出手指，捏起其中一片被撕碎的五線譜殘頁。\n\n那不是印刷的樂譜，而是用鉛筆手工謄寫的原創手稿。音符寫得極其工整娟秀，而在樂譜的抬頭處，隱約能辨認出四個被淚水模糊的鉛筆字：【獻給母親】。\n\n<u>念舟</u>抬起頭，淡淡地看了那位深情未婚夫一眼：\n\n「趙先生，死者的雙手有投保鉅額保險嗎？」\n\n男子愣了一下，眼底閃過一絲極其短暫的警惕，隨即嘆了口氣：\n\n「語萱是鋼琴家，樂團確實替她的雙手投保了五千萬的意外失能險。陳法醫，您問這個做什麼？」\n\n「沒什麼，只是職業病。」<u>念舟</u>站起身，拍了拍褲管，轉頭看向<u>許書晴</u>與檢察官：\n\n「墜落高度十二米，胸腹部著地導致多發性肋骨骨折與內臟破裂。但在沒有進行內部病理解剖之前，我無法在相驗證明書的死因欄上勾選『自殺』。大體先移送市立殯儀館第四解剖室。」\n\n一個小時後。新北市立殯儀館地下二樓。\n\n冰冷的不鏽鋼解剖台上，黑色的加厚屍袋緩緩拉開。\n\n死者沈語萱靜靜躺在冰冷的鐵板上。\n\n她的長髮披散在肩頭，面容精緻秀麗，但左側額骨凹陷，身上原本一塵不染的米白色絲綢連身裙，已經被深紅色的血跡浸透了大半。\n\n然而，最引人注目的，是她的雙手。\n\n那是一雙修長、纖細、骨節分明的手掌。十根手指如同比翼的白鴿般優雅美麗，指甲修剪得極其圓潤乾淨，沒有塗抹任何指甲油。即便此刻毫無生氣地搭在冰冷的鐵板上，依然像是一件上帝精心雕琢的藝術品。\n\n「嘖嘖嘖，這雙手真的是老天賞飯吃耶。」\n\n站在三公尺外的實習助理<u>阿達</u>，一邊往防護口罩裡塞薄荷葉，一邊忍不住小聲嘀咕：\n\n「剛剛送大體過來的那位豪門未婚夫，哭得有多慘啊！開著保時捷，全身都是名牌，聽說是某家大金控的獨生子……唉，這麼漂亮又有才華的鋼琴家，嫁入豪門前途一片光明，到底有什麼想不開要跳樓自殺啊？」\n\n「<u>阿達</u>，」<u>念舟</u>一邊戴上雙層乳膠手套，一邊冷冷地開口，「在解剖室裡，所有的『想不開』，通常都只是活人為了掩蓋真相而編造的劇本。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>走到解剖台前，依照慣例，對著死者微微躬身：\n\n「得罪了，沈小姐。」\n\n隨後，<u>念舟</u>伸出右手，輕輕握住了死者冰冷柔軟的右手手腕，食指按向橈動脈，同時翻轉手掌檢查腕關節與掌面有無防禦性傷痕。\n\n指尖隔著薄薄乳膠，觸碰到死者手腕的瞬間——\n\n「嗡————！」\n\n青銅古鐘的沉重轟鳴，第三次在<u>念舟</u>的顱骨正中央轟然激盪！\n\n胸口鎖骨下方的灼熱沙漏，如同被注入了一股滾燙的熔岩，第三個一百六十八小時，無縫接軌啟動！\n\n下一秒，一道高分貝、充滿了驚恐與崩潰的年輕女聲，在<u>念舟</u>耳畔驟然炸響：\n\n「啊啊啊啊啊啊——！放開我！別碰我的手！」\n\n只見一個半透明、穿著米白絲綢長裙的年輕女孩靈魂，如同受驚的小鹿般從解剖台上一躍而起，整個人飄在半空中，死死將自己的雙手護在胸口前！\n\n女孩一臉驚恐地看著<u>念舟</u>手裡那柄寒光閃閃的解剖刀，長髮在陰風中瘋狂飛舞，尖叫聲穿透力十足：\n\n「這位醫師！你拿刀子要做什麼？！我的手投保了五千萬！我是要在國家音樂廳獨奏的！你絕對不能切斷我的正中神經和肌腱！不能切啊！」\n\n<u>念舟</u>的手停在半空中。\n\n他揉了揉被震得嗡嗡作響的耳膜，面無表情地深吸了一口氣，從容不迫地拿起了游標卡尺：\n\n「沈語萱小姐，第一，妳從十二公尺高處墜落，胸主動脈破裂，頸椎第二節粉碎性骨折。妳現在已經徹底過期了，保險公司只會理賠身故保險金，不會理賠手部失能險；第二，妳的神經和肌腱目前全都處於停止供血狀態，就算我用手術刀把它們切成麵條，妳也感受不到半點疼痛。」\n\n半空中的女孩猛地僵住了。\n\n她低下頭，看著自己透明無暇的十指，又茫然地看著解剖台上那個滿身血污、躺在冰冷鐵板上的自己。\n\n「我……我真的……」\n\n女孩的眼眶瞬間紅了，透明的嘴唇劇烈發顫。\n\n但出乎<u>念舟</u>意料的是，女孩的臉上沒有剛死之人的迷茫，反而爆發出一股刻骨銘心的憤怒與絕望！\n\n她猛地撲到<u>念舟</u>面前，透明的雙手死死抓住虛空，朝著<u>念舟</u>歇斯底里地哭喊起來：\n\n「法醫先生！你聽我說！我沒有自殺！我根本就沒有跳樓！」\n\n「是他……是他把我推下去的！是趙宇恆那個畜生把我推下去的啊！」\n\n站在一旁記錄數據的<u>阿達</u>，看著<u>念舟</u>對著空氣發呆，冷不丁打了個寒顫：「念、<u>念舟</u>哥？你怎麼又定格了？是不是沈小姐的靈魂在跟妳抗議啊……」\n\n「安靜，<u>黃志達</u>，記錄死者腕部骨骼完整度。」<u>念舟</u>頭也不回地喝止，目光卻冰冷而專注地鎖定在半空中的沈語萱身上。\n\n「趙宇恆推妳的？」<u>念舟</u>壓低了聲音，從牙縫裡吐出這幾個字。\n\n「對！就是他！」\n\n沈語萱哭得整個人在半空中劇烈發抖，透明的淚珠無聲地飄散在空氣中：\n\n「他根本就不是什麼深情的富二代！他背著我在外面養小三，還在地下期貨輸了幾千萬！他盯上了我父母留給我的那棟新店老宅，還有我名下的海外信託基金！」\n\n女孩死死捂著自己的胸口，聲音哽咽得令人心碎：\n\n「昨天晚上，他在琴房逼我簽署信託轉移授權書。我拒絕了，我說我要跟他解除婚約……他就瘋了一樣掐住我的脖子，把我往陽台拖！」\n\n「地面上那些撕碎的樂譜是怎麼回事？」<u>念舟</u>冷靜地追問。\n\n提到樂譜，沈語萱的整顆靈魂彷彿被生生撕裂開來，發出了一聲絕望至極的哀鳴：\n\n「那是……那是我媽媽留給我唯一的東西啊……」\n\n沈語萱跪在虛空中，雙手顫抖地抓著自己的長髮：\n\n「我媽媽是個清潔工……我小時候家裡好窮好窮，住在基隆八堵的漏水平房裡。我媽媽為了讓我學鋼琴，冬天清晨四點去幫各大商業大樓洗樓梯，雙手凍到全是裂開的血口子，手指關節變形發黑……她省吃儉用整整十年，才買了一台二手老鋼琴給我……」\n\n沈語萱眼中的悲痛如同一片汪洋大海：\n\n「我媽媽三年前因肺癌過世了。臨走前，她在病床上哼了一首小時候每天哄我睡覺的童謠……我花了兩年時間，把那首童謠改編成鋼琴協奏曲《山櫻花搖籃曲》，打算在下個月國家音樂廳的獨奏會上當作壓軸壓軸曲目，彈給我天上的媽媽聽……」\n\n女孩哭得上氣不接下氣，透明的身軀幾乎要崩散開來：\n\n「可是昨天晚上……趙宇恆那個混蛋，為了逼我妥協，他當著我的面，把那疊手稿撕得粉碎！他踩著我媽媽的心血罵那是鄉巴佬的垃圾！我衝上去搶……他就把我從天台護欄上，狠狠推了下去！」\n\n沈語萱猛地抬起頭，那雙原本彈奏過無數世界名曲的純淨眼眸，此刻滿是哀求與淚水：\n\n「陳法醫……我不能背著『自殺』的罪名離開這個世界……」\n\n「我媽媽一輩子都在為我受苦，她最大的驕傲就是我能堂堂正正、堅強勇敢地活著……如果她知道我是『自殺』死的，她在天上會有多心痛、有多自責啊？！」\n\n「求求你……求求你一定要幫我找出證據……向全世界證明……我沒有自殺！我是被殺的！」\n\n安靜的解剖室裡，只有福馬林的刺鼻氣味在流淌。\n\n<u>念舟</u>靜靜地看著這個痛哭流涕的天才女孩。\n\n他知道，活人的世界是殘酷的。在法庭上，法官不會聽死者的口供，檢察官更不可能採信一個通靈法醫的片面之詞。\n\n要推翻「自殺」的結論，必須拿出鐵證如山的物證。\n\n「墜樓前，妳和他發生過激烈肢體衝突，對不對？」<u>念舟</u>冷靜地開口。\n\n沈語萱愣愣地點了點頭：「我……我撲上去搶樂譜的時候，他抓著我的頭髮，我拼命反抗……」\n\n<u>念舟</u>低下頭，將無影燈的聚光焦點，全部打在死者那雙被稱為「五千萬名琴之手」的纖細手指上。\n\n他戴著放大鏡，拿起精密的微型不鏽鋼解剖鑷，一寸一寸、極其耐心地檢查著死者的指甲邊緣。\n\n在右手中指與無名指的指甲縫最深處——\n\n藉著強烈的光源，<u>念舟</u>敏銳地捕捉到了一抹肉眼幾乎難以辨識的深灰色羊毛纖維，以及深嵌在指甲角質層下方、極微量的皮屑微物！\n\n「找到了。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>的嘴角，緩緩勾起了一抹冷酷而堅決的弧度。\n\n「趙先生身上穿的那件高級定制西裝，正好是深灰色的純羊毛面料。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>放下鑷子，看著半空中止住哭泣、滿眼期待的女孩靈魂，聲音沉靜得如同出鞘的利刃：\n\n「沈小姐，妳的十根手指，不僅能彈奏<u>蕭邦</u>與李斯特。」\n\n「在死後的第七天裡，它們也是親手把兇手送進監獄的致命凶器。」\n\n---\n\n### 💡 故事知識小百科：自縊索溝與徒手扼死（他殺）之病理鑑別（Hanging vs. Manual Strangulation）\n\n典型自縊的勒痕索溝通常呈「馬蹄形」，在頸前喉結上方受力最重，兩側沿下顎向後上方斜行，在枕部或耳後繩結處開放中斷；而徒手扼頸或繩索勒殺他殺時，索溝多呈水平閉合狀，深度均勻且常伴隨抓擦痕與甲狀軟骨上角骨折。此外，真性生活反應伴隨的索溝邊緣表皮剝脫出血與紅斑，是法醫識破偽裝上吊假象、揭開殺人滅口真相的關鍵證據。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 5: The Wealthy Pianist Deemed a \"Suicide\"\n\nTuesday, 3:15 PM. Qingshan Villa Estate, Xindian District, New Taipei City.\n\nThis was an ultra-exclusive, heavily guarded luxury residential enclave nestled against rolling hills and winding waters. Autumn sunlight filtered through the dense bald cypress groves, casting dappled leaf shadows across the broad, pristine asphalt road.\n\nHowever, outside a modern minimalist three-and-a-half-story white villa, blinding yellow police cordon tape fluttered violently in the wind.\n\nDown upon the granite landscaped courtyard below the villa, a dark, shocking pool of congealed blood had already dried, its edges soaking several trampled, ruined white rose petals.\n\nForensic Pathologist Chen Nian-Zhou gripped his heavy stainless-steel field investigation kit, ascending the stairs toward the rooftop terrace on the top floor.\n\nThis terrace had been converted into a panoramic glass piano conservatory boasting spectacular vistas. At the very center of the conservatory rested a Steinway concert grand piano worth millions, its ivory and ebony keys radiating a cool, aristocratic sheen in the sunlight.\n\nThe sliding glass doors of the music room were flung wide open, fronted by a tempered-glass balustrade approximately 1.2 meters high. Currently, the district prosecutor and Detective Investigator Xu Shu-Qing were inspecting the scene beside the railing.\n\n\"The preliminary scene findings are very straightforward,\"\n\nThe prosecutor adjusted his rimless glasses, looking down at his notebook entries:\n\n\"The victim is Shen Yu-Xuan, twenty-six years old, a renowned young concert pianist. Around 11:00 AM this morning, she was discovered fallen in the ground-floor courtyard by a part-time cleaning lady arriving for her shift. On the tea table inside the conservatory lay three prescription bottles of Prozac, a half-empty bottle of red wine, and copious shredded sheet music scattered across the floor. In the wastebasket, investigators recovered a handwritten note reading: 'I can no longer play the sound you desire. These hands are so exhausted.'\"\n\nThe prosecutor turned to gaze toward a young man standing just outside the perimeter, impeccably tailored in an expensive black bespoke suit with reddened eyes:\n\n\"Mr. Zhao, when was the last time you saw Miss Shen alive?\"\n\nThe young man drew out a snow-white linen handkerchief, dabbing at non-existent tears at the corner of his eyes, his voice catching with practiced, pitch-perfect grief:\n\n\"Last night... around ten. She was a perfectionist artist who demanded the impossible from herself. Her solo recital at the National Concert Hall was scheduled for next month, and she spent over twelve hours a day practicing for the past half-year, frequently battling sleepless anxiety... Last night, her emotions spiraled into a furious row with me. To give her space to calm down, I returned to my downtown flat... I never imagined... I never dreamed she would take her own life like this...\"\n\nClutching his handkerchief tight, his shoulders trembled faintly, painting the portrait of a heartbroken fiancé shattered by the loss of his beloved:\n\n\"Prosecutor, Yu-Xuan cherished elegance and dignity above all else in life... If the inquest confirms this was suicide by fall, please expedite the release of her remains. I wish to lay her to rest with utmost decorum, sparing her the indignity of an autopsy...\"\n\n\"Rest assured, Mr. Zhao. We will proceed strictly by legal protocol,\" the prosecutor nodded.\n\nStanding to one side with her case file, Xu Shu-Qing's brow was knit tight. Her instincts screamed that something was subtly discordant about this scene, yet between the latched interior doors, the half-drained wine glass, and the suicide note matching the victim's handwriting, every surface indicator pointed toward a textbook suicide driven by depression.\n\nAt that moment, Nian-Zhou approached, gloved in white.\n\nHe knelt by the glass balustrade, inspecting the subtle smudges along the railing rim, before glancing down at the shredded fragments of sheet music littering the floor.\n\nReaching down, Nian-Zhou picked up a single torn stave of manuscript.\n\nIt was not a commercial score, but an original composition painstakingly drafted in pencil. The musical notes were penned with delicate, elegant precision, and across the header, four faint pencil words were barely discernible through dried water stains: [Dedicated to Mother].\n\nLifting his eyes, Nian-Zhou cast an impassive glance at the grieving fiancé:\n\n\"Mr. Zhao, were the victim's hands insured for a substantial policy?\"\n\nThe man froze for a fraction of a second, an ephemeral flash of wariness darting across his eyes before dissolving into a heavy sigh:\n\n\"Yu-Xuan was a concert pianist; the philharmonic orchestra indeed took out a fifty-million-dollar accidental disability policy on her hands. Doctor Chen, why do you ask?\"\n\n\"Nothing. Just an occupational hazard,\" Nian-Zhou stood up, brushed his knees, and turned to Xu Shu-Qing and the prosecutor:\n\n\"Fall height twelve meters, blunt impact to the thorax and abdomen causing multiple rib fractures and internal organ lacerations. However, prior to an internal pathological autopsy, I will not check the 'Suicide' box on the death certificate. Transport the body to Autopsy Suite 4 at the Municipal Mortuary first.\"\n\nOne hour later. Basement level 2, New Taipei City Funeral Parlor.\n\nUpon the cold stainless-steel dissection slab, the heavy black body bag was slowly unzipped.\n\nThe deceased, Shen Yu-Xuan, lay motionless upon the frigid metal.\n\nHer long dark hair cascaded over her shoulders, her features delicate and refined, though her left frontal bone was depressed, and her pristine ivory silk dress was largely drenched in dark crimson stains.\n\nYet what commanded the eye above all were her hands.\n\nThey were a pair of slender, elongated, exquisitely articulated hands. Ten fingers graceful as twin white doves, her nails trimmed round, neat, and unpainted. Even resting lifeless upon cold steel, they resembled a masterpiece sculpted by the divine.\n\n\"Tsk, tsk, tsk, hands like that are truly blessed by the heavens,\"\n\nStanding three meters back, intern assistant Ah-Da stuffed fresh mint leaves into his surgical mask while muttering under his breath:\n\n\"That wealthy fiancé who brought the body in cried like the world was ending! Drives a Porsche, head-to-toe designer clothes, supposedly the sole heir to a mega-financial holding group... Sigh, a pianist this gorgeous and talented, on the brink of marrying into high society with a glittering future—what could possibly drive her to jump off a roof?\"\n\n\"Ah-Da,\" Nian-Zhou pulled on his double layer of latex gloves, speaking coldly, \"in an autopsy suite, all 'incomprehensible despair' is usually just a script concocted by the living to conceal the truth.\"\n\nApproaching the table, Nian-Zhou bowed slightly toward the dead girl in customary respect:\n\n\"Forgive the intrusion, Miss Shen.\"\n\nThen, Nian-Zhou extended his gloved right hand, gently taking the dead girl's cool, supple right wrist, pressing his index finger to the radial artery while rotating the palm to check the wrist joint and volar surface for defensive wounds.\n\nThrough the thin latex, his fingertips brushed the skin of her wrist—\n\n“HUMMMMM————!”\n\nThe resonant toll of an ancient bronze bell detonated with shocking force right at the core of Nian-Zhou's skull for the third time!\n\nBeneath his collarbone, the searing hourglass flared as if doused in molten magma—the third 168-hour countdown seamlessly ignited!\n\nIn the very next instant, a piercing, hysterical young woman's screech exploded right beside Nian-Zhou's ear:\n\n\"Aaaaaaaah——! Let go of me! Don't touch my hands!\"\n\nA translucent spirit of a young woman in an ivory silk gown sprang from the autopsy slab like a terrified fawn, hovering mid-air and clutching her hands frantically to her bosom!\n\nTerror etched across her face as she beheld the gleaming scalpel in Nian-Zhou's grasp, her long hair whipping wildly in the phantom gale as her shrill cry resonated with piercing force:\n\n\"Doctor! What are you doing with that blade?! My hands are insured for fifty million! I am supposed to perform a solo recital at the National Concert Hall! You cannot sever my median nerve and tendons! You cannot cut them!\"\n\nNian-Zhou's hand halted mid-air.\n\nRubbing his buzzing ear, he drew a deep, long-suffering breath and picked up the vernier caliper with unruffled calm:\n\n\"Miss Shen Yu-Xuan, first of all: you plummeted from a height of twelve meters, suffering a ruptured thoracic aorta and a comminuted fracture of the C2 vertebra. You are now thoroughly expired; the insurance company will only pay out accidental death benefits, not hand disability compensation. Second: all blood circulation to your nerves and tendons has ceased; even if I julienned them into noodles with my scalpel, you wouldn't feel an ounce of pain.\"\n\nThe girl hovering in the air froze solid.\n\nShe lowered her gaze to her flawless, transparent fingers, then looked blankly at her blood-soaked shell lying upon the cold metal slab.\n\n\"I... am I really...\"\n\nHer spectral eyes turned crimson in an instant, her translucent lips trembling violently.\n\nYet to Nian-Zhou's surprise, what surfaced upon her face was not the customary disorientation of the newly dead, but an incandescent, bone-deep fury and despair!\n\nShe threw herself directly before Nian-Zhou, her translucent hands clawing at empty space, crying out with hysterical anguish:\n\n\"Doctor! Listen to me! I did not commit suicide! I never jumped!\"\n\n\"It was him... it was that monster Zhao Yu-Heng who shoved me off!\"\n\nRecording data nearby, Ah-Da watched Nian-Zhou staring blankly into empty air and shivered uncontrollably: \"B-Brother Nian-Zhou? Why did you freeze up again? Is Miss Shen's ghost protesting against you...\"\n\n\"Silence, Huang Zhi-Da. Document the integrity of the carpals,\" Nian-Zhou snapped without turning his head, his cold, razor-sharp gaze locked firmly upon Shen Yu-Xuan in mid-air.\n\n\"Zhao Yu-Heng pushed you?\" Nian-Zhou murmured through gritted teeth.\n\n\"Yes! It was him!\"\n\nShen Yu-Xuan wept, her entire form trembling violently as translucent tears dissolved into the cold air:\n\n\"He was never some devoted, gentle heir! He was cheating on me behind my back, and he lost tens of millions in underground futures trading! He set his sights on the ancestral house in Xindian left by my parents, and the overseas trust fund under my name!\"\n\nClutching her phantom chest, her voice fractured with heart-wrenching agony:\n\n\"Last night, he cornered me in the conservatory, demanding that I sign a power of attorney transferring the trust. I refused, telling him I was breaking off our engagement... He flew into a psychotic rage, grabbed me by the throat, and dragged me toward the balcony!\"\n\n\"What about the shredded sheet music on the floor?\" Nian-Zhou pressed with clinical composure.\n\nAt the mention of the sheet music, Shen Yu-Xuan's soul seemed torn asunder, unleashing an agonizing wail of despair:\n\n\"That was... that was the only treasure my mother left me in this world...\"\n\nKneeling in mid-air, Shen Yu-Xuan clutched her hair with trembling hands:\n\n\"My mother was a cleaning lady... When I was little, our family was desperately poor, living in a leaky shanty in Badu, Keelung. To pay for my piano lessons, my mother washed stairwells in commercial high-rises at four in the freezing winter mornings. Her hands were cracked with raw bloody sores, her knuckles swollen and blackened... She scraped and saved for ten relentless years just to buy me a second-hand upright piano...\"\n\nThe sorrow in her eyes was vast as an ocean:\n\n\"My mother died of lung cancer three years ago. Before she passed, she hummed the lullaby she sang every night in my childhood from her hospital bed... I spent two whole years arranging that melody into a piano concerto called 'The Mountain Cherry Lullaby,' intending it as the grand finale of my recital at the National Concert Hall next month, playing it for my mother in heaven...\"\n\nChoking on her tears, her translucent form nearly dissolved under the weight of grief:\n\n\"Yet last night... that bastard Zhao Yu-Heng tore those manuscript sheets to shreds right in front of my eyes to break my resolve! He stamped on my mother's legacy, sneering that it was peasant trash! When I lunged forward to reclaim them... he shoved me violently over the balcony railing!\"\n\nShen Yu-Xuan jerked her head up, those pure eyes that had once commanded world masterpieces now drowning in tears and desperate supplication:\n\n\"Doctor Chen... I cannot leave this world branded with the shame of 'suicide'... \"\n\n\"My mother spent her entire life suffering for my sake; her greatest pride was seeing me live with head held high, courageous and strong... If she knew I died a 'suicide,' how shattered, how tortured by guilt would she be in heaven?!\"\n\n\"I beg of you... you must help me find proof... prove to the entire world... that I never took my own life! I was murdered!\"\n\nInside the silent autopsy suite, only the pungent stench of formalin drifted through the air.\n\nNian-Zhou gazed quietly at this sobbing young prodigy.\n\nHe knew all too well that the mortal world was merciless. In a court of law, a judge would never hear the testimony of the dead, nor would a prosecutor entertain the claims of a psychic coroner.\n\nTo overturn the ruling of suicide, there had to be irrefutable physical evidence.\n\n\"Before the fall, you had a violent physical struggle with him, didn't you?\" Nian-Zhou asked with absolute calm.\n\nShen Yu-Xuan nodded through tears: \"I... when I lunged to save the music, he grabbed my hair, and I fought back with everything I had...\"\n\nNian-Zhou lowered his gaze, directing the concentrated beam of the shadowless surgical lamp directly onto the delicate hands hailed as \"the fifty-million-dollar masterpiece.\"\n\nWearing a magnifying loupe, he took up a precision micro-dissection forceps, examining the margins of the deceased's fingernails inch by meticulous inch.\n\nDeep beneath the nail folds of her right middle and ring fingers—\n\nUnder the intense illumination, Nian-Zhou's sharp eyes caught a minute, nearly imperceptible trace of dark grey wool fiber, alongside microscopic fragments of epithelial tissue lodged firmly under the subungual keratin layer!\n\n\"Found it.\"\n\nA cold, resolute smirk curved the corner of Nian-Zhou's lips.\n\n\"The bespoke luxury suit Mr. Zhao wore today happens to be pure wool in dark grey.\"\n\nSetting down the forceps, Nian-Zhou met the gaze of the spectral girl hovering above, her weeping stilled, her eyes overflowing with sudden hope. His voice rang out like an unsheathed blade:\n\n\"Miss Shen, your ten fingers were meant not only to play Chopin and Liszt.\"\n\n\"In the seven days after your death, they are also the lethal weapon that will personally drag your murderer behind prison bars.\"\n"},{"id":2,"rawContent":"# 第六章：留在指甲縫裡的第二個人\n\n深夜十一點三十分。新北市立殯儀館，地下二樓解剖室。\n\n無影燈散發著雪白而刺眼的強光，將不鏽鋼解剖台照得一片通亮。\n\n法醫<u>陳念舟</u>佩戴著高倍率手術放大鏡，手裡捏著一柄極其精密的眼科微型不鏽鋼鑷子，整個人的身軀凝固得如同一尊石雕。\n\n「鑷子、載玻片、無菌棉棒。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>的聲音低沉得幾乎沒有任何起伏。\n\n站在一旁的實習助理<u>阿達</u>屏住呼吸，連大氣都不敢喘一口，輕手輕腳地將貼好條碼標籤的無菌證物管遞了過去。\n\n鑷子的尖端在強光下反射出一抹冷冽的銀光。<u>念舟</u>的手指穩定得如同高精度的工業機械手臂，小心翼翼地探入死者沈語萱右手中指的指甲褶襞深處。\n\n伴隨著一記極其微弱的阻力，那抹深灰色的纖維被精準地夾了出來，輕輕置入載玻片上的甘油固定液中。隨後，<u>念舟</u>又用微型棉棒，在指甲角質層下方反覆旋轉刮取，採集到了微量的肉眼幾乎不可見的淡黃色皮屑組織。\n\n「呼……」\n\n直到兩根無菌證物管被徹底密封，<u>念舟</u>才緩緩直起僵硬酸痛的腰背，摘下了放大鏡。\n\n飄在半空中的沈語萱靈魂，一直安安靜靜地注視著這一切。\n\n她看著自己那雙曾經在施坦威鋼琴上飛舞的雙手，此刻被棉棒擦拭著指尖，透明的眼眸中翻湧著難以言喻的悲哀與震撼：\n\n「陳法醫……這些小小的毛線和皮屑……真的能抓到他嗎？」\n\n「在法醫物證學裡，這叫做『洛卡德物質交換定律』。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>一邊將證物管裝進冷藏採樣袋，一邊摘下染血的外層手套：\n\n「只要兩個物體發生接觸，就必然會產生微量物質的轉移與交換。兇手可以偽造自殺遺書，可以擦掉天台門把上的指紋，但他無法阻止自己身上的毛料纖維嵌進妳的指甲，更無法阻止自己的表皮細胞在受到劇烈抓撓時被生生剝離。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>低頭看著解剖台上的大體，眼神平靜而銳利：\n\n「更何況，妳留給他的禮物，遠遠不止這點微物。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>伸出右手，輕輕按向死者那纖細白皙的頸部。\n\n在無影燈的高角度側光照射下，死者的喉結兩側，隱隱浮現出兩道極其微弱、若隱若現的淺褐色皮內出血斑。\n\n「<u>阿達</u>，照相機，垂直九十度對焦頸部。」<u>念舟</u>冷冷下令。\n\n「來了！」<u>阿達</u>立刻舉起專業單眼相機，對準死者的頸部「卡嚓、卡嚓」連拍數張。\n\n<u>念舟</u>拿起游標卡尺，低聲念出精準的病理數據：\n\n「死者舌骨大角右側有零點三公分的點狀皮下溢血，左側甲狀軟骨上角呈現壓迫性骨折。這是標準的生前機械性扼痕——兇手在將她推下天台之前，曾經用單手死死掐住她的咽喉，造成大腦短暫缺氧昏迷。」\n\n半空中的沈語萱猛地捂住自己的脖子，眼中再次浮現出昨夜墜樓前那場噩夢般的窒息感，痛苦地閉上了眼睛。\n\n「如果是一心求死的跳樓自殺，死者的頸部絕對不可能在墜落前就出現甲狀軟骨骨折。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>利落地拉起屍袋拉鍊，拉下口罩，露出了那張掛著兩團深重黑眼圈、卻冷酷如鐵的臉龐：\n\n「<u>阿達</u>，把病理組織切片連夜送去法醫研究所化驗科，要求加急DNA序列比對。我現在去刑警大隊。」\n\n午夜十二點四十分。新北市刑警大隊，重案組辦公室。\n\n整層樓燈火通明，空氣裡瀰漫著濃烈的菸草味、泡麵香氣，以及鍵盤瘋狂敲擊的劈啪聲。\n\n女刑警<u>許書晴</u>正把兩條修長的長腿架在辦公桌邊緣，手裡捏著一罐早就喝乾的能量飲料，對著電腦螢幕上的通聯紀錄皺眉苦思。\n\n在她桌上的卷宗夾裡，塞滿了檢察官發來的督辦照會，以及趙氏金控法務團隊遞交的「請求儘速發還遺體火化聲請書」。\n\n「砰。」\n\n一只沉甸甸的牛皮紙公文袋，毫無預兆地直接拍在了<u>許書晴</u>的鍵盤正中央。\n\n<u>許書晴</u>嚇了一跳，猛地抬頭，看見了穿著黑色防風外套、眼眶充血的<u>陳念舟</u>。\n\n「陳法醫？大半夜的不回去睡覺，你來我們重案組查哨啊？」<u>許書晴</u>揉了揉酸痛的太陽穴，沒好氣地打趣道。\n\n「把妳抽屜裡的免死金牌收起來，準備立案抓人。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>拉開旁邊的旋轉椅，面無表情地坐了下來，將一張彩色列印的解剖相片推到了她面前：\n\n「新店青山鎮墜樓案，正式排除自殺可能，定性為他殺。」\n\n<u>許書晴</u>的眼神瞬間銳利起來，整個人像一頭嗅到血腥味的母豹般挺直了腰背：\n\n「你找到翻案的鐵證了？」\n\n「頸部甲狀軟骨生前骨折，舌骨局部出血，證實墜樓前存在嚴重的扼頸窒息行為。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>伸出食指，重重敲了敲桌面上的鑑識報告：\n\n「更致命的是這個——在死者右手中指與無名指縫深處，採集到了外來男性的上皮細胞，以及微量的深灰色澳洲美利諾純羊毛纖維。纖維的經緯編織紋理與色號，與趙宇恆昨晚在現場穿的那套價值三十萬的英國定制西裝完全吻合。」\n\n<u>許書晴</u>倒吸了一口涼氣，雙眼爆發出無比興奮的光芒：\n\n「那個王八蛋！我就知道他昨晚在那裡演痛哭流涕的時候，眼神一直在往樓下的花園飄！他根本不是在悲傷，他是在確認庭院裡有沒有留下痕跡！」\n\n<u>許書晴</u>猛地抓起桌上的車鑰匙和筆記本：\n\n「我昨晚調取了社區的門禁車牌辨識系統。趙宇恆聲稱他昨晚十點就離開了新店別墅，但實際上，他的保時捷跑車直到昨晚十一點四十分，才從後山的側門悄悄開出去！他有整整一個半小時的完全不在場證明真空！」\n\n飄在<u>念舟</u>身後的沈語萱靈魂，看著兩人在燈火通明的辦公室裡一唱一和、抽絲剝繭地還原真相，原本蒼白冰冷的眼眸中，悄然落下了兩行滾燙的淚水。\n\n她飄到<u>許書晴</u>桌旁那份屬於自己的生平資料前。\n\n檔案上貼著一張她穿著黑色晚禮服、在鋼琴前微笑的宣傳照，旁邊是一行用鉛筆寫下的文字：【被害人母親：基隆清潔隊聘僱工，林秀琴（歿）】。\n\n沈語萱伸出虛幻的手指，輕輕撫摸著照片上母親的名字，聲音輕得如同微風：\n\n「陳法醫……許警官……謝謝你們……」\n\n「我媽媽生前常常跟我說，正義可能會走得很慢，但只要妳坐得正、行得端，老天爺總會看見的……」\n\n<u>念舟</u>端起<u>許書晴</u>桌上剛泡好的熱茶抿了一口，神色依舊冰冷，但眼底深處卻透著一抹不易察覺的柔和：\n\n「老天爺看不看得到我不知道，但新北地檢署的顯微鏡，一定看得到。」\n\n翌日上午九點整。新北市立殯儀館，相驗解剖辦公室。\n\n走廊上傳來了昂貴皮鞋踏在磨石子地面上的脆響，伴隨著兩名中年律師低沉而強勢的交談聲。\n\n辦公室的大門被推開。\n\n涉案未婚夫趙宇恆在兩名西裝革履的大律師陪同下，快步走了進來。\n\n今天的趙宇恆換了一套深藍色的休閒西裝，頭髮梳得油光水滑，手腕上戴著數百萬的百達翡麗名錶，眼底雖然帶著幾分刻意營造的憔悴，但舉手投足間卻充滿了豪門闊少的傲慢與壓迫感。\n\n「陳法醫，許偵查佐。」\n\n領頭的資深大律師推了推金絲眼鏡，將一份厚厚的法律文件拍在桌上，語氣強硬：\n\n「我們是趙氏金控的代表律師。依據《刑事訴訟法》規定，家屬對死因無疑義者，檢察機關應於相驗完畢後儘速發還大體。我們趙先生今天親自過來，是為了領取沈語萱小姐的相驗屍體證明書，並辦理火化許可。趙家已經包下了金寶山最好的墓園，請院方不要再以任何行政程序拖延，徒增家屬悲痛。」\n\n趙宇恆站在一旁，適時地垂下眼皮，嘆了口氣：\n\n「陳法醫，語萱生前那麼愛美……讓她在冰庫裡躺著，我每分每秒都在心如刀割啊……」\n\n坐在辦公桌後的<u>陳念舟</u>，連頭都沒有抬一下。\n\n他慢條斯理地整理著桌上厚厚的一疊解剖圖譜，隨後從抽屜裡抽出了一張白色的文件，輕輕推到了桌子正中央：\n\n「趙先生既然急著火化，那就請在這一張《家屬領具屍體切結書》上簽個名吧。」\n\n趙宇恆眼中閃過一抹難掩的狂喜，隨即快步上前，伸出右手從西裝口袋裡掏出萬寶龍鋼筆，準備在文件上簽字。\n\n然而，就在他俯下身、將右手衣袖往前伸展的瞬間——\n\n<u>念舟</u>銳利如鷹隼般的眼眸，猛然捕捉到了一抹異常！\n\n在趙宇恆右手腕關節上方三公分處、原本被名錶錶帶與襯衫袖口遮掩的手臂內側，隱隱露出了一道約三公分長、塗抹了消炎藥膏卻依然泛著暗紅色血痂的抓痕！\n\n<u>念舟</u>的嘴角勾起了一抹極其冰冷的弧度。\n\n他突然伸手，一把按住了趙宇恆即將落筆的鋼筆筆尖！\n\n「陳法醫？你這是什麼意思？！」旁邊的律師立刻大聲抗議。\n\n趙宇恆也是臉色一沉，惱羞成怒地抽回手：\n\n「<u>陳念舟</u>，你不過是個小法醫，不要太過分了！」\n\n「趙先生，」<u>念舟</u>緩緩站起身，高大挺拔的身軀投下一道迫人的陰影，眼神冰冷得如同手術刀尖：\n\n「這份切結書，你簽不了了。」\n\n就在這時，辦公室的大門被「砰」地一聲再次推開！\n\n<u>許書晴</u>身穿防彈背心，帶著四名荷槍實彈的重案組刑警大步邁入，將整間辦公室的出口死死封鎖！\n\n<u>許書晴</u>手裡高高舉起一張蓋著地檢署大印的紅色公文，聲音洪亮如雷，響徹整棟大樓：\n\n「趙宇恆先生！新北地檢署已於今早八點三十分，正式將青山鎮墜樓案變更為『故意殺人罪』立案偵辦！」\n\n「這是檢察官緊急簽發的《刑事鑑定強制採樣許可書》！」\n\n<u>許書晴</u>一步踏上前，冰冷的手銬在陽光下泛著刺骨的光芒，目光死死盯著趙宇恆手腕上的暗紅抓痕：\n\n「請你脫下外套，把雙手伸出來。」\n\n「沈語萱小姐的指甲，現在要向你討回屬於她的一點東西。」\n\n趙宇恆臉上的偽裝在一瞬間土崩瓦解，整個人踉蹌著後退了半步，臉色慘白如紙！\n\n飄在天花板上的沈語萱，看著眼前這張狼狽不堪、原形畢露的猙獰面孔，在無聲的晨光之中，終於露出了如釋重負的淚光。\n\n---\n\n### 💡 故事知識小百科：洛卡德物質交換定律與微量 STR-DNA 分析（Locard's Exchange Principle & STR-DNA Profiling）\n\n近代法庭科學之父艾德蒙·洛卡德提出著名的「物質交換定律」：凡物體發生接觸，必定伴隨微量物質的轉移與互換。被害人在遭受暴力侵害與近身格鬥時，指甲縫深處極易刮取並嵌留加害人的皮膚脫落角質細胞、皮脂與汗液；現代法醫 DNA 實驗室利用聚合酶連鎖反應（PCR）擴增技術與短相鄰重複序列（STR）基因座分析，能以百億億分之一的極高排除率鎖定兇手遺傳標記。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 6: The Second Person Beneath the Fingernails\n\n11:30 PM. Autopsy Suite, Basement Level 2, New Taipei City Funeral Parlor.\n\nThe surgical shadowless lamps radiated a blazing, sterile white glare, casting a stark brilliance over the stainless-steel dissection slab.\n\nForensic Pathologist Chen Nian-Zhou wore high-magnification surgical loupes, holding an ultra-fine ophthalmic micro-dissection forceps in his grip, his entire posture as motionless as a sculpted statue.\n\n\"Forceps, glass slides, sterile swabs.\"\n\nNian-Zhou's voice was a low, even murmur devoid of inflection.\n\nStanding beside him, intern assistant Ah-Da held his breath, scarcely daring to inhale, gently handing over sterile evidence vials labeled with barcode stickers.\n\nThe tips of the micro-forceps flashed with a cold silver gleam beneath the intense light. Steady as a precision industrial robotic arm, Nian-Zhou's fingers delicately probed deep into the nail folds of deceased Shen Yu-Xuan's right middle finger.\n\nWith a minute fraction of resistance, that single dark grey fiber was teased out with surgical precision, placed gingerly onto the glycerol mounting medium atop the glass slide. Then, using a micro-swab, Nian-Zhou rotated and scraped repeatedly beneath the subungual keratin layer, harvesting microscopic trace quantities of pale yellow epidermal tissue nearly invisible to the naked eye.\n\n\"Phew...\"\n\nOnly after both sterile evidence vials were hermetically sealed did Nian-Zhou slowly straighten his stiff, aching spine, slipping off the surgical loupes.\n\nHovering quietly in mid-air, the spirit of Shen Yu-Xuan had watched every step in rapt silence.\n\nShe gazed down upon those hands that had once flown across Steinway piano keys, now being wiped at the fingertips by cotton swabs, an indescribable wave of sorrow and awe swelling in her translucent eyes:\n\n\"Doctor Chen... can these tiny threads and skin flakes... really bring him down?\"\n\n\"In forensic trace evidence, this is known as 'Locard's Exchange Principle,'\"\n\nStowing the vials into a refrigerated sampling pouch, Nian-Zhou stripped off his outer blood-flecked gloves:\n\n\"Whenever two objects come into contact, a mutual transfer and exchange of trace physical matter is inevitable. The killer could forge a suicide note, could wipe down the brass handles on the terrace doors, but he could never prevent the wool fibers of his suit from embedding under your nails, nor could he stop his epithelial cells from peeling away when you clawed him in desperate resistance.\"\n\nLooking down at the corpse on the table, Nian-Zhou's eyes were calm yet piercingly sharp:\n\n\"What is more, the gift you left him extends far beyond these trace particles.\"\n\nReaching out with his gloved right hand, Nian-Zhou gently touched the dead girl's slender, porcelain neck.\n\nUnder the high-angle oblique illumination of the surgical lamp, two exceedingly faint, hazy subcutaneous hemorrhagic bands materialized faintly on either side of her thyroid cartilage.\n\n\"Ah-Da, digital camera, perpendicular ninety-degree macro focus on the anterior neck,\" Nian-Zhou commanded curtly.\n\n\"Right away!\" Ah-Da raised the professional SLR camera, snapping multiple high-resolution photos with crisp, rapid shutter clicks.\n\nPicking up the digital caliper, Nian-Zhou recited the exact pathological dimensions under his breath:\n\n\"Point-three-centimeter punctate subcutaneous hemorrhage on the right greater horn of the hyoid bone; compression fracture on the left superior horn of the thyroid cartilage. This is textbook antemortem mechanical throttling—the perpetrator used a single hand to violently strangle her throat before pitching her over the balustrade, inducing acute cerebral hypoxia and transient loss of consciousness.\"\n\nFloating in mid-air, Shen Yu-Xuan instinctively clutched her throat, the nightmare of suffocation from the night before surging back as she closed her eyes in phantom agony.\n\n\"In a genuine leap to end one's own life, a victim's neck would never exhibit an antemortem fracture of the thyroid cartilage prior to impact,\"\n\nZipping the heavy body bag shut with fluid efficiency, Nian-Zhou pulled down his surgical mask, revealing a pale face burdened with dark circles yet cold as tempered iron:\n\n\"Ah-Da, deliver the histology tissue cassettes to the Institute of Forensic Medicine's toxicology and genetics lab overnight for expedited DNA sequencing. I am heading to the Criminal Investigation Corps.\"\n\n12:40 AM. Major Crimes Division, New Taipei City Police Department.\n\nThe entire floor blazed with fluorescent light, the air thick with stale cigarette smoke, instant noodle steam, and the relentless clatter of mechanical keyboards.\n\nDetective Xu Shu-Qing had her long legs propped on the edge of her desk, clutching an empty energy drink can while scowling at call detail records glowing on her monitor.\n\nStacked inside the manila folder on her desk were expedited supervisory memos from the district prosecutor and a formal petition for urgent body release for cremation submitted by Zhao Financial Holding's legal team.\n\n\"Thud.\"\n\nA heavy manila evidence packet slammed without warning right across the center of Xu Shu-Qing's keyboard.\n\nStartled, Shu-Qing jerked her head up to find Chen Nian-Zhou standing before her in his black windbreaker, his eyes shot through with red veins.\n\n\"Doctor Chen? Not sleeping at this hour—did you drop by Major Crimes to inspect the night shift?\" Shu-Qing rubbed her aching temples, teasing him dryly.\n\n\"Put away the cremation petition in your drawer and gear up to make an arrest,\"\n\nPulling out a swivel chair, Nian-Zhou sat down without expression, sliding a glossy color autopsy photo across her blotter:\n\n\"The Qingshan Villa fall case: suicide is formally ruled out. Reclassified as homicide.\"\n\nShu-Qing's eyes snapped razor-sharp, sitting up straight like a tigress catching the scent of blood:\n\n\"You uncovered smoking-gun physical evidence?\"\n\n\"Antemortem fracture of the thyroid cartilage and localized hyoid hemorrhage, proving violent manual strangulation prior to the plunge,\"\n\nNian-Zhou jabbed an index finger firmly against the forensic sheet:\n\n\"Even more devastating is this: beneath the subungual spaces of the victim's right middle and ring fingers, we isolated foreign male epithelial cells, accompanied by microscopic Australian Merino pure wool fibers in dark charcoal grey. The weave pattern, ply count, and dye profile match perfectly with the three-hundred-thousand-dollar bespoke British suit Zhao Yu-Heng wore at the scene last night.\"\n\nShu-Qing sucked in a sharp breath, her eyes blazing with triumphant fury:\n\n\"That rotten scoundrel! I knew it! When he put on that tearful performance last night, his eyes kept darting toward the garden below! He wasn't mourning; he was checking if he left anything behind in the flowerbeds!\"\n\nSnatching her car keys and field notepad from the desk, Shu-Qing shot to her feet:\n\n\"I pulled the gated community's license plate recognition logs early this morning. Zhao Yu-Heng claimed he left the Xindian estate at ten last night, but his Porsche didn't sneak through the rear mountain exit until 11:40 PM! He has a ninety-minute void in his alibi!\"\n\nHovering behind Nian-Zhou, Shen Yu-Xuan's spirit watched the two of them dismantling the web of lies in the brightly lit precinct, two trails of hot, translucent tears spilling down her pale cheeks.\n\nShe drifted to the edge of Shu-Qing's desk, gazing upon her biographical case sheet.\n\nAffixed to the paper was a promotional photograph of her smiling before a grand piano in an evening gown, beside a line penned in pencil: [Victim's Mother: Contract Sanitation Worker, Keelung Cleaning Squad, Lin Xiu-Qin (Deceased)].\n\nShen Yu-Xuan raised an ethereal finger, gently tracing her mother's name on the paper, her voice soft as a passing breeze:\n\n\"Doctor Chen... Detective Xu... thank you both so very much...\"\n\n\"My mother always told me when I was little that justice might travel slowly, but as long as you walk upright with an honest heart, the heavens will eventually bear witness...\"\n\nNian-Zhou picked up the freshly brewed hot tea on Shu-Qing's desk, taking a sip, his face impassive as ever, yet a faint warmth flickered in the depth of his gaze:\n\n\"Whether heaven bears witness, I cannot say. But the microscopes of the New Taipei District Prosecutors Office certainly do.\"\n\n9:00 AM the following morning. Autopsy Administration Office, New Taipei City Funeral Parlor.\n\nThe crisp cadence of expensive Italian leather shoes clicking over terrazzo tile echoed down the hallway, accompanied by the low, overbearing conversation of two middle-aged corporate attorneys.\n\nThe office door swung wide.\n\nFlanked by two sharp-suited legal counsels, the suspect fiancé Zhao Yu-Heng strode in briskly.\n\nToday, Zhao Yu-Heng wore an impeccably styled navy leisure blazer, his hair slicked back with pomade, a multimillion-dollar Patek Philippe watch gleaming on his wrist. Though he wore an engineered veneer of grief, every posture radiated the arrogant condescension of an untouchable heir.\n\n\"Doctor Chen, Detective Xu,\"\n\nThe lead corporate counsel adjusted his gold spectacles, slapping a thick sheaf of legal motions onto the counter, his tone commanding and aggressive:\n\n\"We represent Zhao Financial Holdings. Pursuant to the Code of Criminal Procedure, where the family raises no objections to the cause of death, the prosecuting authority must release the body post-inquest without delay. Mr. Zhao has arrived in person to receive Miss Shen Yu-Xuan's autopsy death certificate and finalize the cremation permit. The Zhao family has chartered the premier mausoleum plot at Chin Pao San; we insist the mortuary cease all bureaucratic delays that only compound the family's grief.\"\n\nStanding beside him, Zhao Yu-Heng lowered his eyelids with practiced melancholy, letting out a heavy sigh:\n\n\"Doctor Chen, Yu-Xuan was so devoted to grace... having her lie in a cold freezer tears my heart to pieces with every passing second...\"\n\nSitting behind the desk, Chen Nian-Zhou didn't even bother lifting his chin.\n\nHe methodically gathered a stack of gross pathology anatomical diagrams, then withdrew a single white document from his desk drawer, sliding it smoothly to the center of the desk:\n\n\"Since Mr. Zhao is in such a hurry to cremate, please sign your name here on this 'Family Body Release Indemnity Agreement.'\"\n\nA flash of poorly concealed triumph darted across Zhao Yu-Heng's eyes. Stepping forward hastily, he reached into his breast pocket for his Montblanc fountain pen, leaning over to sign the line.\n\nHowever, the split second he bent forward and extended his right sleeve—\n\nNian-Zhou's hawk-like eyes caught an unmistakable anomaly!\n\nThree centimeters above Zhao Yu-Heng's right wrist joint—partially hidden beneath the luxury watchband and French cuff—was an angry scratch three centimeters long, smeared with antiseptic ointment yet still glistening with dark dried blood!\n\nA bone-chilling smirk curled Nian-Zhou's lips.\n\nHe shot his hand out, pressing his palm firmly over the tip of Zhao Yu-Heng's pen just before it struck paper!\n\n\"Doctor Chen?! What is the meaning of this?!\" The corporate lawyer erupted in immediate indignation.\n\nZhao Yu-Heng's face darkened, jerking his hand back with barely suppressed fury:\n\n\"Chen Nian-Zhou, you're merely a minor forensic examiner. Do not cross the line!\"\n\n\"Mr. Zhao,\" Nian-Zhou slowly rose to his feet, his tall, imposing frame casting an intimidating shadow, his eyes cold as a scalpel's edge:\n\n\"This release agreement—you won't be signing it.\"\n\nJust then, the office door slammed open with a concussive crash!\n\nDressed in a tactical ballistic vest, Xu Shu-Qing led four heavily armed Major Crimes detectives into the room, sealing every exit with absolute authority!\n\nHeld high in Shu-Qing's grip was a formal crimson-sealed legal warrant, her voice booming like thunder through the corridors:\n\n\"Zhao Yu-Heng! As of 8:30 AM this morning, the New Taipei District Prosecutors Office has officially reclassified the Qingshan Villa fall as an active investigation for 'Intentional Homicide'!\"\n\n\"This is a court-ordered Compulsory Forensic Sampling Warrant signed by the lead prosecutor!\"\n\nStepping forward, Shu-Qing pulled cold steel handcuffs from her tactical belt, her gaze boring like a drill into the dark red claw marks on his wrist:\n\n\"Take off your jacket and extend both hands.\"\n\n\"Miss Shen Yu-Xuan's fingernails have a few things they need to take back from you.\"\n\nEvery shred of Zhao Yu-Heng's manufactured composure crumbled to ash in an instant. Stumbling backward a half-pace, his face turned as white as a corpse!\n\nFloating near the ceiling, Shen Yu-Xuan looked upon that unmasked, grotesque face of panic, and amidst the silent morning light, her tears of boundless vindication finally fell.\n"},{"id":3,"rawContent":"# 第07章：未曾彈完的蕭邦夜曲\n\n新北市刑警大隊第一偵訊室的空氣冷得像結了霜。\n\n隔音海綿包裹的牆壁泛著灰白，單向透視玻璃後方站著神情凝重的<u>張巡官</u>，而偵訊桌的正對面，豪門長子<u>趙凌雲</u>已經換上了一身乾淨的深藍色訂製襯衫，兩名身價千萬的王牌刑案律師一左一右端坐身側，神情倨傲得彷彿他們只是來巡視自家的私人會所。\n\n「張隊長，我再次重申，我當事人<u>趙凌雲</u>先生手臂上的傷痕，是前幾天在自家陽台修剪玫瑰花時被刺枝劃傷的。」左側的資深律師將一份厚重的法律意見書推向前，鏡片後方的眼神帶著老練的譏誚，「你們無端扣押趙先生超過六小時，甚至在未出具正式鑑定書前就強行限制人身自由，這在法庭上完全經不起檢驗。若十分鐘內不放人，我們將立刻向地方法院聲請提審，並對新北地檢署提出國家賠償與妨害名譽訴訟。」\n\n坐在中央的<u>趙凌雲</u>神色從容，甚至優雅地撫平了袖口的皺褶，嘴角掛著一抹若有若無的冷笑。他那雙保養得宜的手指輕輕敲擊著桌面，發出沉悶的聲響，眼神裡滿是看著螻蟻垂死掙扎的輕蔑。\n\n偵訊室的鐵門「吱呀」一聲被推開。\n\n走進來的不是手足無措的刑警，而是換回了皺巴巴卡其褲與夾克的<u>陳念舟</u>。他的手裡沒有拿警棍或手銬，只有一疊剛從刑事警察局法醫化驗室印出來、還帶著雷射印表機餘溫的紙張，以及一個密封在透明防潮盒裡的黑色隨身碟。\n\n<u>念舟</u>拉開鐵椅坐下，濃烈的老舊解剖室福馬林味與廉價長壽菸味瞬間在密閉的偵訊室內擴散開來。他沒有看律師，也沒有看那份昂貴的法律意見書，只是靜靜地抬起布滿血絲的雙眼，直視著<u>趙凌雲</u>那張偽善的臉孔。\n\n「修剪玫瑰？」<u>念舟</u>的聲音低沉而沙啞，像是磨砂紙刮過粗糙的木頭，「趙先生家裡的園藝品種真特別，長出來的玫瑰刺，還懂得精準分泌人類男性的皮脂腺上皮細胞。」\n\n兩名律師臉色驟然一變。\n\n<u>念舟</u>將第一張檢驗報告拍在桌面上。\n\n「法務部法醫研究所與刑事局 DNA 實驗室的急件加急比對結果，十五分鐘前剛出爐。」<u>念舟</u>伸出一根被菸燻得微黃的食指，重重地點在報告最下方的十六組 STR 基因位點數據上，「從死者<u>白芷晴</u>右手中指殘破的甲床深處，我們以無菌生理食鹽水與超音波震盪萃取出的微量上皮細胞。十六組基因型完全吻合，排除非<u>趙凌雲</u>本人遺留的機率，是百億億分之一。」\n\n<u>趙凌雲</u>敲擊桌面的手指猛地僵住，眼角抽搐了一下。\n\n「陳法醫，DNA 污染在鑑識實務上屢見不鮮！」右側較年輕的律師立刻拔高聲調反駁，「<u>芷晴</u>是趙先生的未婚妻，兩人同居、親密接觸，指甲縫裡殘留未婚夫的皮屑完全合情合理，這根本不能作為殺人證據！」\n\n「別急，王牌律師，我還沒說完。」<u>念舟</u>冷冷地打斷他，將第二張高倍立體顯微鏡的創口斷層比對圖推了過去。\n\n「如果是日常生活親密接觸，落入指甲縫的只會是鬆散脫落的表皮角質死皮。但在<u>白芷晴</u>指甲縫裡刮出來的，是帶有真皮乳頭層微血管紅血球、以及活體生長層細胞的組織碎塊。」<u>念舟</u>指著顯微照片上那團暗紅色的組織，「換句話說，這是人在承受劇烈痛苦與窒息掙扎時，用盡全身殘存力氣，硬生生從活人肉體上狠狠摳挖下來的新鮮皮肉。」\n\n偵訊室裡死寂一片，只剩下空調運轉的低鳴。\n\n「接著，是趙先生手腕上那道所謂的『玫瑰花刺傷』。」<u>念舟</u>將照片翻到下一頁，露出<u>趙凌雲</u>被強行拍照存證的手腕特寫，「植物刺傷的物理特徵是點狀刺入、或單向線狀撕裂，伴隨植物汁液與花刺倒鉤造成的表皮內陷；但你手腕上的傷痕，創緣有反向卷曲的表皮襟翼，創溝深淺呈不對稱波浪狀，那是人類指甲弧形扣入、遭遇腕關節肌肉劇烈扭轉所留下的抓痕。而那道抓痕的弧度與寬度，與<u>白芷晴</u>齊根折斷的右手中指甲片，在三維光學掃描儀下重疊誤差小於零點零二公釐。」\n\n<u>趙凌雲</u>的臉色開始由白轉青，額角滲出了一層細密的冷汗。\n\n「最後，是這個。」<u>念舟</u>將隨身碟插進筆記型電腦，轉向<u>趙凌雲</u>，「你案發當晚宣稱十一點前就回到信義區豪宅睡覺，但陽明山別墅門口的私人道路監監視器雖然被你拔了電源，山腳下自來水廠的防汛高解析度紅外線鏡頭卻在凌晨一點十四分，拍到了你名下的銀灰色保時捷下山。更巧的是，<u>白芷晴</u>頸部殘留的羊毛纖維，是英國 Savile Row 訂製店專利混紡的 Super 180s 喀什米爾羊毛，染色批號全球僅三件——其中一件，現在就掛在張隊長扣押的你家更衣室衣架上，衣領處甚至還驗出了<u>白芷晴</u>生前噴灑的同一款白茶香水。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>合上資料夾，發出一聲清脆的「啪」響，宛如法官敲下的法槌。\n\n「<u>趙凌雲</u>，她臨死前死命抓著你，不是為了求生，她是為了用自己的指甲和血肉，替自己寫下最後的死亡證明。」<u>念舟</u>的聲音冷得刺骨，「你徒手掐死她，再偽裝成自縊，用鋼琴吊燈的絲繩侮辱她視若生命的音樂。你以為金錢和律師能買下所有謊言，但在法醫學面前，死人的身體從不說謊。」\n\n「夠了！閉嘴！」\n\n<u>趙凌雲</u>猛地從鐵椅上彈起，雙手重重拍在鐵桌上，那副偽裝出來的豪門名流面具徹底碎裂，雙眼布滿暴怒的血絲，聲嘶力竭地吼道：「那個不知好歹的賤女人！她懂什麼？那三千萬音樂基金本來就是我趙家的資源，我拿去週轉公司資金有什麼錯？她竟然敢拿著帳本威脅我要召開記者會退婚！她以為她是誰？不過是一個三重大拜拜路邊攤長大的窮酸女，靠我捧她才能站在國家音樂廳的台上！我給了她名分、給了她地位，她居然想毀了我！」\n\n兩名律師臉色慘白地癱坐在椅子上，連制止當事人的力氣都沒了。\n\n單向玻璃後的鐵門被推開，張隊長帶著兩名持槍刑警大步邁入，鋥亮的手銬在日光燈下閃爍著冰冷的光芒。\n\n「<u>趙凌雲</u>，你涉嫌殺人罪，現行犯逮捕，不准保釋。」張隊長聲音如雷，手銬「喀嚓」一聲狠狠扣上了<u>趙凌雲</u>顫抖的手腕。\n\n看著<u>趙凌雲</u>被狼狽拖出偵訊室，<u>陳念舟</u>只是疲憊地閉上眼，揉了揉刺痛的太陽穴。\n\n走廊的轉角處，空氣微微泛起一陣寒意。\n\n<u>念舟</u>睜開眼，看見<u>白芷晴</u>單薄的身影正靜靜站在陰影裡。手銬扣上真兇那一刻，籠罩在她魂魄周圍的青黑怨氣已經散去大半，但她的眼眶裡依然蓄滿了晶瑩的靈魂淚光，那雙殘破翻折的十指無助地垂在身側。\n\n「<u>念舟</u>……謝謝你。」<u>芷晴</u>的聲音輕得像一陣風，帶著解脫，卻又藏著無盡的遺憾，「但我……好想再彈一次琴……」\n\n<u>念舟</u>低下頭，看了看腕錶。\n\n晚上九點十五分。\n\n距離死後第七天的子時午夜——牛頭馬面拘魂的絕對死線——只剩下最後兩個小時又四十五分鐘。\n\n「<u>老張</u>，」<u>念舟</u>轉過身，看向剛走出來的<u>張巡官</u>，神情嚴肅得近乎懇求，「今晚能幫我借到新北市藝文中心演奏廳的鑰匙嗎？半個小時就好。」\n\n張隊長愣了一下，看著<u>念舟</u>那雙布滿血絲卻堅定異常的眼睛，又看了看物證袋裡那本被淚水與折痕磨損的琴譜，隨即嘆了口氣，掏出車鑰匙：「你這瘋子……走吧，那裡的館長是我警大同學，我用局長的名義押證件跟他說。」\n\n夜色籠罩的新北街頭飄著冰冷的細雨，警車一路鳴笛疾馳，在十點整停在了寂靜無人的藝文中心大門口。\n\n巨大的演奏廳內漆黑一片，唯有穹頂的一盞應急檢修燈灑下孤寂的冷光，正正打在舞台中央那架黑色的史坦威三角鋼琴上。\n\n琴蓋倒映著空無一人的紅色觀眾席，沉寂得像一座巨大的黑曜石墓碑。\n\n「<u>念舟</u>，這架琴……我和媽媽以前進不來。」<u>芷晴</u>飄浮在鋼琴旁，伸出半透明的手指，顫抖著想要撫摸琴鍵，指尖卻一次次穿透黑白鍵盤，「小時候，我們家住在三重重新橋下漏水的鐵皮屋裡。媽媽一個人做三份工，清晨去果菜市場搬菜，下午去成衣廠車縫，晚上去夜市洗碗……」\n\n<u>念舟</u>走上舞台，拉開琴凳坐下，將那本被小心塑封的泛黃琴譜輕輕攤開在譜架上。\n\n那是<u>白芷晴</u>手寫的樂譜。樂譜的開頭是<u>蕭邦</u>著名的《降E大調夜曲，作品九之二》，但在中段最華麗的裝飾音處，音符卻巧妙地轉調，融入了一首極其質樸、溫柔的台灣童謠旋律。\n\n樂譜右下角，用鉛筆工整地寫著一行娟秀的小字：《獻給媽媽的搖籃曲：山櫻花與夜曲》。\n\n「媽媽的雙手長滿了老繭，指關節因為冬天洗菜凍得變形粗大。」<u>芷晴</u>的魂魄坐在<u>念舟</u>身邊，眼淚一滴滴落在琴鍵上，化作虛無的微光，「她省吃儉用，把每一枚十塊硬幣、每一張皺巴巴的百元鈔票，都塞進一個印著喜餅圖案的鐵盒子裡。小學三年級那年，她終於湊齊了三萬塊，買回了一台二手泛黃的山葉直立鋼琴……」\n\n「她看不懂五線譜，但每當我練琴練到哭的時候，她就會坐在板凳旁，一邊給我揉手指，一邊哼這首《山櫻花搖籃曲》哄我睡覺。」<u>芷晴</u>哽咽著，聲音破碎得令人心碎，「她臨終前在安寧病房裡對我說，她這輩子最驕傲的事，就是看到我穿著漂亮禮服在舞台上彈琴……她說她會在天上聽著。」\n\n舞台兩側的陰影中，空氣突然劇烈扭曲。\n\n伴隨著沉重而古老的馬蹄聲與鐵鏈碰撞聲，身披黑風衣的老牛與手持拘魂平板的阿馬無聲無息地自虛空中顯現。\n\n老牛臉上的威嚴肅穆前所未有，他罕見地沒有掏出香菸，只是低頭看了一眼泛著幽綠光芒的拘魂簿。\n\n「陳法醫，」阿馬的電子音罕見地放低了音量，帶著一絲嘆息，「距離子時拘魂，還有三十八分鐘。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>深吸了一口氣，抬起那雙長年握解剖刀、指尖長著硬繭的手，懸在黑白琴鍵上方。\n\n「我高中畢業後就沒碰過琴了，」<u>念舟</u>苦笑了一聲，轉頭看向身邊的<u>白芷晴</u>，「指法肯定很爛，妳別嫌棄。」\n\n「不會的……」<u>芷晴</u>含著淚微笑，將她那雙虛幻、透明、指甲折斷的手，輕輕覆蓋在<u>念舟</u>粗糙的手背上，「<u>念舟</u>，閉上眼睛，感受音符的呼吸……我帶著你彈。」\n\n第一個和弦輕輕落下。\n\n《降E大調夜曲》溫柔悠揚的旋律在空曠死寂的音樂廳內緩緩流淌開來。\n\n起初，<u>念舟</u>的觸鍵有些生澀僵硬，但在<u>芷晴</u>靈魂的指引下，琴音漸漸變得柔和、深沉，如同夜幕下波光粼粼的湖面。\n\n旋律流轉，到了樂譜的轉折處，<u>蕭邦</u>那古典浪漫的憂傷悄然褪去，取而代之的是帶著台灣泥土氣息與母親溫度的童謠旋律。\n\n那琴音裡，有三重巷弄裡下雨時鐵皮屋頂的滴答聲；有果菜市場凌晨濕漉漉的水氣；有洗碗槽裡刺骨冰水浸泡雙手的隱忍；有餅乾鐵盒裡硬幣碰撞的清脆聲響；更有一個平凡瘦弱的母親，用整個生命托舉起女兒音樂夢想的無盡深情。\n\n空無一人的音樂廳裡，琴聲宛如實質的溫暖潮水，滌蕩著每一個角落。\n\n舞台陰影處，抱著勾魂鎖鏈的老牛緩緩閉上了眼睛，神情肅穆；而一向跳脫搞笑的阿馬，平板螢幕上的綠光也柔和地閃爍著，靜靜聆聽這跨越生死的人間絕響。\n\n樂曲漸漸走向終章。\n\n那是最後一個長音，溫柔得像母親粗糙的手掌最後一次拂過女兒的長髮，又像一朵在寒冬風雨中盛開的山櫻花，終於迎來了春日的陽光。\n\n琴音落下，餘音在音樂廳的穹頂盤旋良久，最終歸於寧靜。\n\n舞台中央，時鐘的秒針悄然跨過了夜間十一點整，子時已至。\n\n<u>白芷晴</u>從琴凳上站起身來。\n\n在這一刻，奇蹟般的光芒籠罩了她的全身。她脖頸上那圈烏黑恐怖的扼痕消失了，右手上齊根翻折的指甲重新變得晶瑩圓潤，她身上那件冰冷的解剖布袍，化作了一襲宛如白天鵝般優雅高貴的純白演奏禮服。\n\n她轉過身，面向<u>陳念舟</u>，雙手交疊在腹前，優雅而莊重地深深鞠了一躬。\n\n「<u>念舟</u>法醫，謝謝你替我申冤，謝謝你讓我彈完了這首曲子。」<u>白芷晴</u>的臉上不再有痛苦與怨恨，唯有一片澄澈明亮的釋然微笑，「媽媽……一定聽到了。」\n\n老牛與阿馬緩緩走上前來。\n\n這一次，老牛沒有亮出那條冰冷沉重的玄鐵鎖鏈，而是從懷中取出了一條柔和的暗紅色引魂絲帶，輕輕搭在<u>白芷晴</u>白皙的手腕上。\n\n「白姑娘，時辰到了。」老牛的聲音低沉而溫和，「令堂在忘川河畔的三生石旁等妳三年了，她給妳燉了熱湯，走吧。」\n\n<u>芷晴</u>眼眶泛紅地點了點頭，回頭最後看了<u>念舟</u>一眼：「陳法醫，請你一定要繼續當法醫……因為你，死人才不會含冤離去。」\n\n「一路好走，白小姐。」<u>念舟</u>站起身，筆挺地站立在鋼琴旁，微微躬身致意。\n\n青煙裊裊，三道身影伴隨著柔和的光暈，漸漸消散在虛空之中。\n\n偌大的演奏廳重歸死寂，唯有一束追光燈靜靜照著黑色的史坦威鋼琴。\n\n<u>念舟</u>緩緩坐回琴凳上，掏出一支長壽菸叼在嘴裡，卻沒有點燃。他從懷裡掏出那本隨身攜帶的黑皮筆記本，在寫著<u>白芷晴</u>名字的那一頁空白處，工整地寫下了一行字：\n\n「案由：自縊（修正為他殺）。死亡原因：扼頸窒息。最後心願：為母親彈奏《山櫻花與夜曲》。狀態：已完成。」\n\n合上筆記本，<u>念舟</u>望著空無一人的觀眾席，長長地吐出了一口夾雜著菸草與福馬林餘味的氣息。\n\n黑夜漫長，但晨光終將刺破陰霾。\n\n---\n\n### 💡 故事知識小百科：指甲生長生理週期與生前抓傷反向捲曲痕跡（Nail Growth Physiology & Defensive Scratch Morphology）\n\n人類手指甲以每月平均約 3 公釐的速度從甲母質向外生長，指甲外傷或橫向斷裂具有明確的時間追溯價值。在激烈防衛抵抗時，被害人指甲嵌入兇手皮肉並向後拉扯，會在兇手皮膚表面形成表皮剝脫與反向卷邊的爪痕力學向量；透過光學三維表面掃描儀比對抓傷溝槽曲率，能與死者指甲殘損的微觀崩裂鋸齒達到物理幾何層面的嚴密嵌合。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 07: The Unfinished Chopin Nocturne\n\nThe air in the first interrogation room of the New Taipei Criminal Investigation Corps was as cold as frost.\n\nThe acoustic foam walls showed a faded grayish-white tint, and behind the one-way glass stood Inspector Zhang with a solemn, stern expression. Directly opposite the interrogation table sat Zhao Lingyun, eldest son of the prestigious family, now changed into a crisp, navy-blue tailored shirt. Flanking him on either side were two top-dollar defense attorneys, seated upright with an arrogant demeanor, as if they had merely dropped by to inspect their private social club.\n\n\"Captain Zhang, I reiterate: the marks on my client Mr. Zhao Lingyun's arm were accidental scrapes from rose thorns while trimming bushes on his balcony a few days ago.\" The senior attorney on the left pushed a thick legal brief forward, a seasoned sneer glinting behind his spectacles. \"You have detained Mr. Zhao without grounds for over six hours, and even forcibly restricted his personal freedom before producing any formal forensic report. This will not hold up in court for a second. If you do not release him within ten minutes, we will immediately petition the District Court for habeas corpus review and file state compensation and defamation lawsuits against the New Taipei District Prosecutors Office.\"\n\nSitting in the center, Zhao Lingyun appeared completely at ease, even casually smoothing down the creases of his cuff with a faint, arrogant smirk playing across his lips. His well-groomed fingers tapped lightly against the table in a steady, dull rhythm, his gaze dripping with disdain, as though watching ants struggle in vain before death.\n\nThe heavy iron door of the interrogation room creaked open.\n\nThe person who stepped inside was not an intimidated detective, but Chen Nianzhou, dressed back in his wrinkled khaki trousers and jacket. He carried no baton or handcuffs in his hands—only a stack of freshly printed lab sheets still warm from the laser printer at the Criminal Investigation Bureau's forensic laboratory, and a black flash drive sealed inside a transparent moisture-proof case.\n\nNianzhou pulled out an iron chair and sat down. Instantly, the thick smell of old morgue formalin and cheap Long Life cigarettes spread through the sealed interrogation room. He glanced neither at the lawyers nor at the lavish legal brief; he simply lifted his bloodshot eyes and stared straight into Zhao Lingyun's hypocritical face.\n\n\"Trimming roses?\" Nianzhou's voice was low and gravelly, like sandpaper scraping across raw lumber. \"Mr. Zhao's garden variety must be truly extraordinary. The rose thorns it grows even know how to precisely secrete human male sebaceous epithelial cells.\"\n\nThe two attorneys' expressions shifted abruptly.\n\nNianzhou slapped the first lab report down onto the steel table.\n\n\"The expedited forensic match from the Ministry of Justice's Institute of Forensic Medicine and the CIB DNA Laboratory came out fifteen minutes ago.\" Nianzhou extended a tobacco-stained index finger and pressed it heavily against the sixteen STR locus profiles at the bottom of the sheet. \"Extracted via sterile saline and ultrasonic agitation from deep within the mangled nail bed of victim Bai Zhiqing's right middle finger were trace epithelial cells. All sixteen STR loci match completely. The statistical probability of these cells originating from anyone other than Zhao Lingyun is one in one hundred quintillion.\"\n\nZhao Lingyun's rhythmic tapping froze instantly, and the corner of his eye twitched.\n\n\"Forensic Pathologist Chen, DNA contamination is commonplace in forensic practice!\" the younger attorney on the right immediately countered in a sharp, raised voice. \"Zhiqing was Mr. Zhao's fiancée! They cohabited and had intimate contact. For dead skin flakes from her fiancé to remain under her fingernails is entirely plausible and reasonable. That cannot possibly stand as evidence of murder!\"\n\n\"Don't be in such a rush, counselor. I'm not finished,\" Nianzhou cut him off coldly, sliding the second sheet—a cross-sectional wound profile taken under a high-power stereomicroscope—across the table.\n\n\"In casual daily intimacy, what collects under fingernails is merely loose, sloughed-off epidermal stratum corneum dead cells. But scraped from Bai Zhiqing's nail bed were tissue fragments containing dermal papillary capillaries with red blood cells and live stratum basale cells.\" Nianzhou pointed to the dark red cluster of tissue on the micrograph. \"In other words, this was fresh, living flesh violently gouged from a living person by someone using every ounce of their dying strength amidst agonizing struggle and asphyxiation.\"\n\nThe interrogation room fell dead silent, save for the low hum of the air conditioner.\n\n\"Next, regarding that so-called 'rose thorn scratch' on Mr. Zhao's wrist.\" Nianzhou flipped to the next page, revealing a forensic macro photograph of Zhao Lingyun's wrist taken during compulsory sampling. \"The physical characteristics of plant thorn injuries are puncture tears or unidirectional linear scratches accompanied by epidermal indentation caused by plant sap and back-curved barbs. But the wound on your wrist features retro-curling epidermal flaps and an asymmetrical undulating groove. That is the hallmark of human fingernails digging in, met by the violent twisting of wrist tendons during a life-or-death struggle. Under a 3D optical profilometer, the contour and width of that scratch groove match Bai Zhiqing's snapped middle fingernail with an error margin of less than zero point zero two millimeters.\"\n\nZhao Lingyun's complexion began to shift from pale to sickly green, and fine beads of cold sweat broke out across his temples.\n\n\"Finally, there is this.\" Nianzhou plugged the flash drive into a laptop and rotated the screen toward Zhao Lingyun. \"You claimed you were already back asleep in your Xinyi District penthouse before eleven on the night of the incident. While you unplugged the private road surveillance camera at the Yangmingshan villa, the flood-control high-resolution infrared camera at the water treatment plant at the base of the hill captured your silver-gray Porsche heading down at one fourteen in the morning. Even more damning: the wool fibers recovered from Bai Zhiqing's neck are a patented Super 180s cashmere-wool blend from a Savile Row bespoke tailor in London, dyed in a proprietary batch limited to only three suits globally. One of them is currently hanging on the rack in your walk-in closet under Captain Zhang's seizure order—and its collar even tested positive for the exact white tea perfume Bai Zhiqing wore in life.\"\n\nNianzhou shut the file folder with a crisp, echoing snap, sounding just like a judge's gavel striking the bench.\n\n\"Zhao Lingyun, she clawed into you before dying not to beg for her life, but to use her own fingernails and your flesh to write her own final death certificate.\" Nianzhou's voice was chillingly sharp. \"You strangled her with your bare hands, staged it as a hanging, and used the silk cord of the piano chandelier to desecrate the music she held dearer than life itself. You believed your wealth and lawyers could purchase any lie. But in forensic science, a corpse never lies.\"\n\n\"Enough! Shut up!\"\n\nZhao Lingyun sprang abruptly from his iron chair, slamming both palms down onto the metal table. His polished aristocratic facade shattered entirely, his eyes bloodshot with frantic rage as he roared hysterically: \"That ungrateful, worthless bitch! What did she know?! That thirty-million-dollar music foundation was my family's money to begin with! What was wrong with using it for company cash flow?! How dare she take the ledgers and threaten to call a press conference to cancel the engagement! Who did she think she was?! Just a dirt-poor street rat raised on temple fair night markets in Sanchong! She only stood on the stage of the National Concert Hall because I groomed and promoted her! I gave her status, I gave her a name, and she wanted to destroy me?!\"\n\nBoth attorneys sank back into their chairs, their faces ash-white, lacking even the strength to restrain their client.\n\nThe steel door behind the one-way glass burst open, and Captain Zhang strode in accompanied by two armed detectives, gleaming steel handcuffs reflecting coldly under the fluorescent lights.\n\n\"Zhao Lingyun, you are under arrest as a flagrant offender for homicide. No bail.\" Captain Zhang's voice boomed like thunder as the cuffs snapped shut around Zhao Lingyun's trembling wrists with a sharp, merciless click.\n\nWatching Zhao Lingyun get dragged out of the interrogation room in disgrace, Chen Nianzhou merely closed his eyes in exhaustion and rubbed his throbbing temples.\n\nAt the corner of the corridor, a faint chill stirred in the air.\n\nNianzhou opened his eyes and saw Bai Zhiqing's slender figure standing silently in the shadows. The moment the handcuffs locked onto the killer, the dark grudge-mist shrouding her soul had mostly dispersed, yet her eyes still brimmed with crystalline spiritual tears, her mangled, broken fingers hanging helplessly at her sides.\n\n\"Nianzhou... thank you,\" Zhiqing whispered, her voice as light as a breeze, filled with release yet carrying boundless sorrow. \"But I... I so wish I could play the piano one last time...\"\n\nNianzhou looked down at his wristwatch.\n\nNine fifteen in the evening.\n\nOnly two hours and forty-five minutes remained until the midnight Zi hour of the seventh day—the absolute deadline when Ox-Head and Horse-Face would claim her soul.\n\n\"Old Zhang,\" Nianzhou turned toward Inspector Zhang, who had just walked out, his expression grave to the point of pleading, \"can you help me borrow the keys to the New Taipei Arts Center concert hall tonight? Just half an hour.\"\n\nCaptain Zhang froze for a moment. He looked into Nianzhou's bloodshot yet resolutely determined eyes, then glanced at the sheet music folder inside the evidence bag—worn by tears and creases. He sighed, fished out his patrol car keys, and said, \"You crazy bastard... Let's go. The center director was my classmate at Central Police University. I'll pledge my badge in the Bureau Chief's name.\"\n\nA cold drizzle drifted through the night over the streets of New Taipei. The patrol car sped through the darkness with sirens flashing, pulling up at the empty, silent Arts Center at ten o'clock sharp.\n\nThe cavernous auditorium was pitch black, save for a single maintenance worklight hanging from the dome, casting a solitary beam of cold light squarely upon the black Steinway concert grand piano at center stage.\n\nThe piano lid reflected the empty rows of red velvet seats, as silent and solemn as a colossal obsidian monument.\n\n\"Nianzhou, this piano... Mom and I could never come in here.\" Zhiqing hovered beside the grand piano, reaching out translucent fingers in a trembling effort to touch the keys, only for her fingertips to pass through the black and white ivory again and again. \"When I was little, we lived in a leaky tin-roof shack beneath Chongxin Bridge in Sanchong. Mom worked three jobs all by herself—hauling produce at the wholesale vegetable market at dawn, operating sewing machines at the garment factory in the afternoon, washing dishes at the night market until midnight...\"\n\nNianzhou stepped onto the stage, pulled out the piano bench, sat down, and gently unfolded the carefully plastic-sealed, yellowed sheet music onto the music stand.\n\nIt was music handwritten by Bai Zhiqing. The score began with Chopin's famed *Nocturne in E-flat Major, Op. 9 No. 2*, but at the climax of the ornate ornamentation in the middle section, the notes ingeniously modulated, blending seamlessly into an immensely tender and rustic Taiwanese lullaby melody.\n\nIn the bottom-right corner of the score, a delicate pencil note was written in neat, elegant handwriting: *A Lullaby Dedicated to Mom: Mountain Cherries and Nocturne*.\n\n\"Mom's hands were covered in thick calluses, her finger joints swollen and deformed from washing vegetables in the bitter winter cold.\" Zhiqing's soul sat beside Nianzhou on the bench, tears dripping one by one onto the keys and dissolving into ethereal flecks of light. \"She pinched every penny, saving every ten-dollar coin and wrinkled hundred-dollar bill inside an old tin cookie box decorated with wedding designs. When I reached third grade, she finally gathered thirty thousand dollars and bought a yellowed, secondhand Yamaha upright piano...\"\n\n\"She didn't know how to read sheet music. But whenever I cried from frustration while practicing, she would sit on the stool beside me, massaging my sore fingers while softly humming this *Mountain Cherry Lullaby* to soothe me to sleep.\" Zhiqing choked up, her voice breaking with heartbreaking sorrow. \"Before she passed away in the hospice ward, she told me the proudest moment of her entire life was seeing me in a beautiful gown playing on stage... She said she would be listening from heaven.\"\n\nIn the shadows on both flanks of the stage, the air suddenly warped violently.\n\nAccompanied by the heavy, ancient clatter of hooves and the clinking of iron chains, Ox-Head in his black trench coat and Horse-Face clutching his glowing soul tablet materialized silently from the void.\n\nOx-Head carried an unprecedented solemnity upon his countenance. For once, he did not reach for a cigarette, merely gazing down at the faint green glow of the underworld registry.\n\n\"Forensic Pathologist Chen,\" Horse-Face's synthesized voice dropped unusually low, laced with a rare sigh, \"thirty-eight minutes remain before the Zi hour claiming.\"\n\nNianzhou took a deep breath. He raised his hands—hands calloused from years of gripping scalpels—and hovered his fingers above the black and white keys.\n\n\"I haven't touched a piano since graduating from high school,\" Nianzhou murmured with a self-deprecating smile, turning toward Bai Zhiqing beside him. \"My fingering is bound to be terrible. Please bear with me.\"\n\n\"You'll do wonderfully...\" Zhiqing smiled through her tears. She gently laid her ethereal, translucent hands with their broken fingernails over the backs of Nianzhou's rough hands. \"Nianzhou, close your eyes and feel the breath of the notes... I will guide your fingers.\"\n\nThe first chord descended softly.\n\nThe gentle, mellifluous melody of the *E-flat Major Nocturne* began to flow quietly through the vast, hollow stillness of the concert hall.\n\nAt first, Nianzhou's keystrokes were somewhat stiff and unpracticed, but guided by Zhiqing's soul, the music grew steadily warmer, deeper, like moonlight rippling across a tranquil lake at midnight.\n\nAs the music developed and reached the transition in the score, the classical romantic melancholy of Chopin quietly gave way, replaced by the earthy Taiwanese melody that carried the scent of home and the warmth of a mother's embrace.\n\nIn that melody lived the steady patter of rain against the corrugated tin roofs of Sanchong alleys; the damp, chilly mist of the fruit and vegetable market before daybreak; the enduring silence of hands submerged in freezing dishwater; the crisp metallic chime of coins dropping into a cookie tin; and above all, the boundless devotion of an ordinary, frail mother who lifted her daughter's musical dreams with the entirety of her humble life.\n\nIn the empty auditorium, the piano notes felt like a tangible wave of warmth, washing through every shadowy corner.\n\nIn the shadows of the wings, Ox-Head held his soul chains and slowly closed his eyes in solemn respect, while the normally boisterous Horse-Face watched silently as the emerald light of his tablet dimmed, both listening in reverence to this farewell song spanning the realms of the living and the dead.\n\nThe melody gently drifted toward its final movement.\n\nIt was a sustained, gentle concluding note, soft as a mother's calloused palm caressing her daughter's hair for the very last time, and like a mountain cherry blossom blooming bravely in the freezing winter wind, finally greeting the first warm rays of spring sunlight.\n\nThe music faded. The final resonance hovered beneath the high vaulted ceiling of the hall for a long time before dissolving into profound peace.\n\nCenter stage, the second hand of the clock quietly ticked past eleven o'clock. The Zi hour had arrived.\n\nBai Zhiqing stood up from the piano bench.\n\nAt that very instant, a miraculous luminescence enveloped her entire form. The hideous black strangulation marks around her throat vanished, her broken, ripped fingernails turned whole, lustrous, and smooth once more, and the cold morgue cloth draped over her dissolved into a pure white evening gown, elegant and proud like a swan in flight.\n\nShe turned toward Chen Nianzhou, crossed her hands gracefully in front of her waist, and bowed deeply with solemn grace.\n\n\"Forensic Pathologist Chen, thank you for clearing my name, and thank you for helping me finish this piece.\" Pain and resentment had completely vanished from Bai Zhiqing's face, replaced by a radiant, serene smile of release. \"Mom... must have heard it.\"\n\nOx-Head and Horse-Face stepped slowly forward.\n\nThis time, Ox-Head did not draw his heavy, frigid iron chains. Instead, he drew from inside his coat a soft ribbon of dark red silk, resting it gently around Bai Zhiqing's fair wrist.\n\n\"Miss Bai, your hour has come,\" Ox-Head said in a deep, gentle voice. \"Your mother has waited for you by the Sansheng Rock at the banks of the Wangchuan River for three years. She has a hot bowl of soup ready for you. Let us go.\"\n\nZhiqing's eyes welled with tears as she nodded, turning back to cast one final look at Nianzhou: \"Forensic Pathologist Chen, please... never stop being a forensic doctor. Because of you, the dead do not depart carrying unavenged wrongs.\"\n\n\"Have a safe journey, Miss Bai,\" Nianzhou said, rising to stand straight beside the piano and bowing his head with deep respect.\n\nAmidst wisps of blue vapor and a warm, fading halo, the three figures gradually dissolved into the boundless void.\n\nThe vast concert hall returned to quiet stillness, with only a solitary spotlight shining down upon the black Steinway grand piano.\n\nNianzhou slowly sat back down on the bench and placed an unlit Long Life cigarette between his lips. From his jacket, he pulled his ever-present black leather notebook, and in the blank space beside Bai Zhiqing's name, he wrote down a neat, deliberate entry:\n\n\"Case Type: Apparent Suicide (Amended to Homicide). Cause of Death: Manual Strangulation Asphyxia. Final Dying Wish: Perform *Mountain Cherries and Nocturne* for her mother. Status: Completed.\"\n\nClosing the notebook, Nianzhou gazed out at the empty auditorium and let out a long breath mingling the scent of tobacco and faint traces of formalin.\n\nThe night is long, but the dawn will always pierce the darkness.\n"},{"id":4,"rawContent":"# 第08章：阿達的平安符與解剖室失竊案\n\n新北市立殯儀館地下一樓的解剖室，深夜裡總是安靜得只剩下排氣扇單調的蜂鳴聲。\n\n牆上的指針指向凌晨一點三十分，剛進法醫室實習滿兩個月的<u>陳敬達</u>——同事口中的「<u>阿達</u>」——正縮在值班台的鐵摺疊椅上，一手端著半涼的統一肉燥泡麵，另一手死命攥著胸前那枚用紅繩串著的大甲鎮瀾宮過爐平安符。\n\n「阿舟老師，」<u>阿達</u>壓低嗓音，喉結緊張地上下滾動，圓圓的娃娃臉上滿是敬畏，「剛才送進第七號冷藏櫃的那位老阿婆……真的只是在三重大同南路的拆遷廢墟裡凍死的無名遊民嗎？我剛才登記遺物編號的時候，總覺得後頸涼颼颼的，好像有人一直站在我背後哈氣……」\n\n坐在解剖報告台前的<u>陳念舟</u>頭也沒抬，手中的鋼筆在相驗初步卷宗上劃出一道俐落的紅線：「低溫凍死常伴隨反常脫衣現象（Paradoxical undressing），但老太太被發現時，身上裹著三層破爛卻整齊的厚棉襖。更重要的是，她後腦枕骨處有一處三公分的挫裂傷，傷口周圍伴隨微量生活反應出血。」\n\n「也就是說……她不是自己路倒凍僵的？」<u>阿達</u>手裡的塑膠叉子僵在半空中。\n\n「她是被人推倒撞擊硬物後，失去行動能力，在攝氏八度的濕冷雨夜裡被活活拋棄在瓦礫堆中失溫致死。」<u>念舟</u>放下筆，揉了揉滿是血絲的雙眼，指尖在泛黃的相驗照片上輕輕一點，「而且，她胸前內袋裡裝著的那只紅色喜餅鐵盒，表面有被強力撬開的痕跡。這不是普通的意外路倒，這是一起偽裝成街友凍斃的故意遺棄致死案。」\n\n話音未落，<u>阿達</u>胸前那枚貼肉佩戴的紅色刺繡平安符，毫無預兆地劇烈發燙起來。\n\n那種燙並非溫水浸泡的暖意，而是像一塊燒紅的炭火直接烙印在皮膚上。<u>阿達</u>痛得「哇」了一聲扯出平安符，只見錦囊邊緣竟冒出一縷肉眼可見的淡青色青煙，符袋上的金線刺繡正迅速被一圈烏黑的香灰焦痕吞噬。\n\n與此同時，走廊盡頭的第七號冰櫃厚重的不鏽鋼門把手，發出了一聲極其清脆的「喀嗒」彈跳聲。\n\n解剖室主照明燈管突然發出一陣刺耳的「滋滋」電流鳴響，隨即整排日光燈驟然熄滅，只剩下天花板四角的綠色逃生緊急照明燈，將整座地下室染上一層詭異慘澹的幽光。\n\n黑暗中，沉重而拖沓的腳步聲從冷藏庫深處一步一步挪了出來，伴隨著塑膠拖鞋在水泥地面上摩擦的沙沙聲，以及一陣若有若無、極其沙啞衰老的婦人啜泣。\n\n「有、有鬼啊！阿舟老師！大甲媽祖顯靈了！平安符燒起來了！」<u>阿達</u>嚇得整個人從椅子上彈起，一頭撞在<u>念舟</u>背後的鐵櫃上，手裡的泡麵湯汁灑了半身，整個人抖得像狂風中的落葉。\n\n<u>念舟</u>沒有動，甚至連眉頭都沒皺一下。他從口袋裡掏出一支長壽菸叼在嘴角，左手熟練地按下打火機，橘紅色的火光在幽綠的房間裡閃爍了一下。\n\n在打火機微弱的火光照耀下，解剖室的鐵門口不知何時多了一道佝僂瘦小的虛影。\n\n那是個滿頭白髮如枯草般凌亂的老婦人，駝著背，身上穿著一件褪色起毛球的碎花舊棉襖，腳上穿著一雙磨穿了鞋底的藍白拖鞋。她的魂魄半透明而虛弱，一雙布滿老人斑與龜裂傷口的枯瘦雙手，正焦急地在空氣中虛抓著，嘴裡不停地喃喃自語：「我的鐵盒子……阿弟的相片……莫拿走……那是阿弟唯一的相片啊……」\n\n<u>念舟</u>靜靜吐出一口青藍色的菸霧，雙眼穿透虛影，低聲道：「老人家，七天之內，<u>陳念舟</u>在的地方，沒人能搶走妳的東西。」\n\n老人家的魂魄猛地一震，那雙渾濁空洞的靈魂之眼望向<u>念舟</u>，隨即顫巍巍地撲通一聲跪倒在地，發出了撕心裂肺的無聲乾號。\n\n「<u>阿達</u>，開備用手電筒。」<u>念舟</u>冷靜地吩咐道，眼底卻掠過一絲前所未有的凌厲，「解剖室有人闖進來了。」\n\n<u>阿達</u>戰戰兢兢地摸出強光手電筒，白色的光柱刺破黑暗，照向了值班台後方的物證暫存鐵櫃。\n\n原本掛著密碼鎖的三號物證箱竟然被液壓剪硬生生鉸斷，櫃門敞開，剛從老婦人遺體內袋取出的那只生鏽喜餅鐵盒、以及一只破爛的藍色帆布背包，已經不翼而飛！\n\n地面的水泥塵埃上，赫然留著幾枚深重的新鮮泥濘鞋印，鞋底花紋呈現特殊的「V」字形交叉防滑紋路，正一路延伸向解剖室後方的運屍坡道逃生門。\n\n「幹！連停屍間的死人遺物都有人敢偷？！」<u>阿達</u>的恐懼瞬間被一股熱血頂替，憤怒地握緊了拳頭，「那老阿婆身上連十塊錢都沒有，就只有那幾張爛紙和破盒子，這賊到底是窮瘋了還是喪盡天良？！」\n\n「那不是普通的小偷。」<u>念舟</u>戴上乳膠手套，蹲下身用強光手電筒照射著地面上的鞋印與刮痕，「鞋印深度左重右輕，步幅約七十五公分，體重大約八十五公斤；鞋底邊緣黏附著極其細緻的黃褐色黏土與高濃度瀝青顆粒，這是三重重新橋下違建拆遷工地特有的基底泥漿。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>用無菌棉花棒輕輕沾取門把上殘留的微量粉末，放在鼻尖嗅了嗅：「還有工業級柴油與高硬度碎石機磨損的金屬粉屑。偷東西的，是那處拆遷工地的現場工頭或怪手司機。」\n\n「他偷那個破鐵盒做什麼？」<u>阿達</u>不解地問。\n\n「因為那只鐵盒裡裝著的，不是錢，而是能證明老太太身分、以及她對那棟老屋擁有合法繼承產權的原始地契與戶籍謄本。」<u>念舟</u>站起身，聲音冷冽如刀，「建商為了強拆老舊違建申請高額容積獎勵，這兩年一直在四處驅趕不肯搬遷的老住戶。老太太無兒無女、神智不清，只要她死成『無名遊民』，名下的老宅就會被當作無主廢棄物直接剷平，數千萬的都更利益就全進了建商的口袋。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>轉向跪在地上的老婦人魂魄，眼神漸漸變得柔和而悲憫：「但是那個工頭沒想到，老太太被推倒後雖然昏迷，卻死死咬著牙爬了幾十公尺，把鐵盒藏在最深處的破棉襖裡，直到被巡邏員警發現送到這裡。」\n\n聽到這裡，老婦人的魂魄劇烈顫抖起來，乾癟的嘴唇哆嗦著，將一段記憶透過靈魂波長直接傳遞進了<u>念舟</u>的腦海。\n\n二十五年前，雲林北港朝天宮廟口。\n\n那是一個香火鼎盛的元宵節夜晚，三歲的孫子「阿弟」在熱鬧的人潮中被一隻陌生的大手悄悄抱走，從此人間蒸發。老阿婆發了瘋似地找遍了全台灣每一個角落，丈夫積勞成疾早逝，她便賣掉了祖產，背著一只破帆布包，靠著撿破爛和在工地幫傭，一路流浪到台北三重，在拆遷區的破鐵皮屋裡一住就是二十年。\n\n她每天清晨出門的第一件事，就是在電線桿上貼尋人啟事；每天晚上睡覺前，都會拿出那個喜餅鐵盒，摸一摸孫子唯一留下的滿月照片，以及當年她在朝天宮求來的兩枚母子平安符。\n\n「阿弟……阿婆把妳弄丟了……」老婦人的哭聲彷彿從深井底傳來，淒涼得令人鼻酸，「阿婆不能走……阿婆走了，阿弟要是找回家……會找不到阿婆……」\n\n<u>阿達</u>站在一旁，眼眶突然徹底紅了。\n\n他低下頭，看著自己手裡那枚被燒焦半邊的平安符，手背上的青筋一根根暴起。\n\n「阿舟老師，」<u>阿達</u>的聲音哽咽而堅定，「這案子，我一定要幫她辦到底。我老家就在北港……我小時候在朝天宮廟埕跑跳的時候，廟門口總是有一個駝背的老阿嬤，不管大雨天還是寒流，都會坐在榕樹下給路過的小孩遞熱薑茶，逢人就拿著一張泛黃的照片問『有沒有看過我家阿弟』……」\n\n<u>阿達</u>抬起頭，淚水在眼眶裡打轉：「那就是她！她是我小時候看過的那位『薑茶阿嬤』！」\n\n<u>念舟</u>拍了拍<u>阿達</u>顫抖的肩膀，眼神深邃：「既然認出來了，就別讓老人家在黃泉路上繼續當無名氏。<u>老張</u>剛好在附近巡邏，我們去把東西拿回來。」\n\n凌晨兩點十五分，三重重新橋下拆遷工地。\n\n狂風捲著冰冷的細雨抽打在破碎的鋼筋與瓦礫堆上，一台巨大的怪手停在工地中央，後方的鐵皮工務所裡亮著一盞昏黃的鎢絲燈泡，隱隱傳出數錢與鐵罐撞擊的聲音。\n\n工務所的木門被張隊長一腳踹開。\n\n身形肥碩的工地主任<u>劉大強</u>正坐在辦公桌前，手裡拿著一把噴燈，試圖將那只撬開的喜餅鐵盒熔成廢鐵，桌上散落著幾張泛黃的地契、一張蓋有北港鎮公所印章的戶籍謄本，以及一張邊角磨損、塑膠膜泛黃的嬰兒滿月照。\n\n「警察！動手就把你銬起來！」張隊長拔槍厲喝，身後的兩名便衣刑警迅速上前制伏了想要跳窗逃跑的工頭。\n\n「長官！誤會啊！這是我在工地的垃圾堆裡撿到的廢鐵！」<u>劉大強</u>被按在桌上，滿臉橫肉劇烈抽搐，大聲嚎叫著，「撿破爛犯法嗎？你們憑什麼抓我？！」\n\n<u>陳念舟</u>緩步走進工務所，<u>阿達</u>緊跟在後。\n\n<u>念舟</u>沒有理會<u>劉大強</u>的叫囂，只是走到桌前，拿起那張被噴燈微焦的嬰兒照片，小心翼翼地吹去上面的灰燼，然後轉向<u>劉大強</u>。\n\n「撿破爛不需要半夜一點翻進新北殯儀館解剖室，用液壓剪破壞公有物證櫃。」<u>念舟</u>從口袋裡拿出一支紫光燈管，照向<u>劉大強</u>那雙沾滿機油的手掌。\n\n在紫外光的照射下，<u>劉大強</u>的十指指尖與袖口上，瞬間亮起了一層刺眼耀眼的青綠色螢光！\n\n「法醫室物證櫃的把手與箱體表面，常年噴塗法醫專用的微量隱形螢光標記粉末（Luminescent Transfer Powder）。」<u>念舟</u>冷冷地盯著臉色慘白的工頭，「只要徒手接觸過，粉末就會嵌入指紋紋路與皮脂腺，三天之內用肥皂洗都洗不掉。」\n\n<u>劉大強</u>看著自己發光的雙手，嘴唇開始劇烈顫抖。\n\n「還有，」<u>念舟</u>指著<u>劉大強</u>腳上那雙沾滿黃泥的鋼頭工作鞋，「你鞋底的『V』字形紋路，與解剖室地板上的泥印完全相符。更致命的是，我們在老太太後腦的挫裂傷口深處，採集到了與你開的那台怪手挖斗邊緣同一成分的重防腐環氧樹脂漆片。你在昨晚暴雨中強行推倒她，看著她倒在泥水裡撞破頭顱，然後狠心鎖上工地大門任由她失溫而死。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>的聲音如同來自地獄的審判：「蓄意強拆、過失致死再轉為遺棄致死，外加深夜侵入公署竊盜物證。<u>劉大強</u>，你這輩子準備在牢裡把牢底坐穿吧。」\n\n<u>劉大強</u>雙腿一軟，徹底癱倒在泥地裡，連一句辯解的話都說不出來。\n\n張隊長押著嫌犯走出工務所，<u>阿達</u>則默默走上前，將散落在桌上的地契、戶籍謄本、以及那張珍貴的照片，一張一張重新收進了那個生鏽的喜餅鐵盒裡。\n\n工務所門外，細雨漸漸停了，東方的天際泛起了一抹魚肚白。\n\n在泥濘的瓦礫堆旁，老阿婆的魂魄靜靜地佇立在清晨的晨霧中。\n\n<u>阿達</u>走上前去，雙手恭恭敬敬地將那只鐵盒捧在胸前，眼淚終於忍不住決堤而出，撲通一聲在老婦人的虛影前跪了下來。\n\n「阿婆……東西找回來了。」<u>阿達</u>泣不成聲，聲音在空曠的廢墟裡迴盪，「地契拿回來了，戶籍拿回來了……阿弟的相片，也好好地在這裡。」\n\n老婦人低下頭，看著那個完好無損的鐵盒，原本滿是驚恐與牽掛的臉上，緩緩綻開了一抹無比溫柔的微笑。\n\n虛空之中，伴隨著古老的蹄聲，身穿黑風衣的老牛與阿馬再次自晨霧中浮現。\n\n老牛嘴裡破天荒地沒有叼菸，神情沉靜地看著跪在地上的<u>阿達</u>與老婦人。\n\n「<u>阿達</u>，」<u>念舟</u>輕聲提醒道，「把你的平安符拿出來。」\n\n<u>阿達</u>愣了一下，連忙從胸口扯出那枚被燒焦半邊的大甲媽祖平安符，連同鐵盒一起高高舉起。\n\n老婦人伸出半透明的手，輕輕撫摸過<u>阿達</u>的頭頂，那觸感冰涼，卻帶著長輩無盡的慈愛與撫慰。\n\n「好孩子……謝謝你……」老婦人的聲音不再沙啞，變得像春風一樣輕柔，「阿弟當年……要是長大，應該也跟你一樣大了吧……」\n\n晨光刺破雲層，金色的朝霞灑在老阿婆的身上。\n\n她身上的破爛棉襖與磨損拖鞋化作了一身乾淨整齊的藍色布衫，駝著的背脊挺直了，臉上的老人斑與風霜皺紋漸漸褪去，露出了慈祥溫暖的容顏。\n\n老牛走上前，手中捧著一盞古樸的引路青燈，對著老婦人微微躬身：「老夫人，苦等二十五年，塵緣已盡。令郎與令夫在奈何橋頭備了清茶，走吧。」\n\n「老牛叔，」<u>阿達</u>抹著眼淚抬起頭，「阿弟呢？阿婆找了一輩子的阿弟……到底在哪裡？」\n\n阿馬翻了翻手裡的電子生死簿，嘆了一口氣，聲音罕見地溫柔：「阿弟當年被拐賣後生了重病，七歲那年就已經先走一步了。但他沒有去投胎，一直乖乖坐在奈何橋邊等阿婆……他們一家，終於要團圓了。」\n\n老阿婆轉過身，朝著<u>念舟</u>與<u>阿達</u>深深一鞠躬，含著幸福的淚水，跟在引路燈後，步履輕盈地走向晨曦深處。\n\n晨霧散去，廢墟上只留下一縷淡淡的檀香氣息。\n\n<u>念舟</u>蹲下身，扶起哭成了淚人的<u>阿達</u>，從口袋裡掏出一包面紙塞進他手裡：「哭夠了就站起來。身為法醫，眼淚要流在心裡，手上握刀的時候，手不能抖。」\n\n「阿舟老師……我知道了。」<u>阿達</u>吸了吸鼻子，用力擦乾眼淚，將那個鐵盒緊緊抱在懷裡，「我會親自替阿婆縫好大體，送她最後一程。」\n\n<u>念舟</u>望著初升的旭日，點燃了嘴裡叼著的長壽菸。\n\n新的一天開始了，而在法醫的相驗筆記本上，又一個漂泊無依的亡魂，終於找到了回家的路。\n\n---\n\n### 💡 故事知識小百科：低體溫凍死「維斯涅夫斯基斑」與反常脫衣現象（Wischnewsky Spots & Paradoxical Undressing）\n\n在低體溫症（Hypothermia）導致的凍死案例中，死者的胃黏膜皺襞深處常可見無數沿血管分佈的黑褐色點狀或條狀黏膜下出血斑，稱為「維斯涅夫斯基斑（Wischnewsky spots）」，為自主神經失調與血管舒縮衰竭的生活反應。此外，在極度失溫瀕死之際，大腦下視丘體溫調節中樞嚴重痲痺，人體會產生劇烈的全身灼熱幻覺，死者往往在死前自主脫去厚重禦寒衣物，此即著名的「反常脫衣現象」。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 08: Ah-Da's Peace Talisman and the Morgue Heist\n\nIn the basement autopsy suite of the New Taipei City Mortuary, the dead of night was always so quiet that only the monotonous droning of the exhaust fans remained.\n\nThe clock hands on the wall pointed to one thirty in the morning. Chen Jingda—known to his colleagues as \"Ah-Da\"—who had just completed two months as a forensic intern, was curled up on an iron folding chair beside the duty desk, holding a lukewarm bowl of Uni-President minced pork instant noodles in one hand while clutching desperately with the other at a Dajia Jenn Lann Temple Mazu peace talisman strung with red cord against his chest.\n\n\"Master Nianzhou,\" Ah-Da murmured in a hushed whisper, his Adam's apple bobbing nervously as his round, boyish face brimmed with awe, \"that elderly grandmother who was just wheeled into Cold Locker Number Seven... was she really just an unidentified vagrant who froze to death in the demolition ruins on Datong South Road in Sanchong? Just now, when I was cataloging her personal effects, my neck felt icy cold, as if someone was standing right behind me exhaling chilled breath...\"\n\nSitting at the autopsy reporting station, Chen Nianzhou did not even lift his head. His fountain pen drew a sharp red underline across the preliminary inquest file: \"Deaths from severe hypothermia are frequently accompanied by paradoxical undressing, but when this elderly woman was found, she was bundled in three layers of ragged yet neatly buttoned heavy padded coats. More crucially, there is a three-centimeter laceration-contusion on the occipital bone at the back of her skull, surrounded by trace intravital hemorrhage.\"\n\n\"Meaning... she didn't just collapse on the street and freeze on her own?\" The plastic fork in Ah-Da's hand froze mid-air.\n\n\"She was pushed and struck a hard object, losing mobility, before being abandoned alive amidst the rubble on a damp, freezing eight-degree rainy night to die of hypothermia.\" Nianzhou set down his pen, rubbed his bloodshot eyes, and gently tapped his fingertip against the yellowed forensic photo. \"Furthermore, the red wedding-cookie tin box tucked inside the inner lining of her coat bears marks of having been forcefully pried open. This is no ordinary accidental collapse; this is an intentional abandonment resulting in death disguised as a homeless freeze.\"\n\nBefore the words had fully landed, the red embroidered talisman worn against Ah-Da's skin suddenly turned scalding hot without the slightest warning.\n\nIt was not the gentle warmth of warm water, but the searing sting of glowing charcoal branded directly onto his flesh. Ah-Da cried out in pain and yanked the talisman out from beneath his shirt, only to see a faint wisp of pale green smoke rising from the edge of the silk pouch, the golden embroidery swiftly consumed by a circle of blackened incense-ash char.\n\nSimultaneously, at the far end of the hallway, the heavy stainless-steel latch of Cold Locker Number Seven emitted a distinct, crisp snapping click.\n\nThe main fluorescent tubes of the autopsy room let out a shrill buzzing whine of electric current, and in the next instant, the entire row of lights abruptly went out, leaving only the greenish emergency exit fixtures at the corners of the ceiling, casting the subterranean chamber in an eerie, pale spectral glow.\n\nIn the darkness, heavy, shuffling footsteps dragged forward step by step from the depths of the cold storage, accompanied by the rustling scrape of plastic slippers against the concrete floor and the faint, raspy weeping of an elderly woman.\n\n\"G-G-Ghost! Master Nianzhou! Dajia Mazu is manifesting! The talisman caught fire!\" Terrified, Ah-Da bounded out of his chair and slammed headfirst into the metal cabinet behind Nianzhou, noodle broth sloshing all over his clothes as he trembled like a leaf in a gale.\n\nNianzhou did not budge, his brow not even twitching. He fished a Long Life cigarette from his pocket, placed it between his lips, and flicked his lighter with his left thumb, a small orange flame flickering in the dim green room.\n\nIlluminated by the lighter's faint glow, a frail, stooped phantom had materialized unnoticed by the iron doors of the autopsy room.\n\nIt was an elderly woman with wild, withered white hair like dry grass, her back severely hunched, dressed in a faded, pilled floral padded jacket and wearing blue-and-white plastic flip-flops with soles worn completely through. Her soul was translucent and feeble. Her withered, wrinkled hands, dotted with age spots and cracked fissures, clutched frantically at the empty air, her lips murmuring in endless distress: \"My tin box... Ah-Di's photo... Don't take it away... That's Ah-Di's only photograph...\"\n\nNianzhou exhaled a stream of blueish-gray smoke, his gaze piercing through the apparition, and spoke in a low voice: \"Elder, within seven days, in any place where Chen Nianzhou stands, no one can steal what belongs to you.\"\n\nThe elderly woman's spirit shuddered violently. Her clouded, hollow spectral eyes turned toward Nianzhou, and then, trembling, she fell to her knees with a thud, letting out a silent, heartbreaking sob.\n\n\"Ah-Da, turn on the backup flashlight,\" Nianzhou instructed calmly, though a razor-sharp glint flashed across his eyes. \"Someone has broken into the autopsy suite.\"\n\nTrembling, Ah-Da produced the high-intensity flashlight. Its beam of white light slashed through the darkness, illuminating the temporary evidence locker behind the duty station.\n\nLocker Number Three, originally secured with a padlock, had been severed clean through with hydraulic bolt cutters. The metal door hung wide open; the rusted cookie tin and the tattered blue canvas backpack retrieved from the elderly woman's inner coat were gone!\n\nOn the concrete dust of the floor were several prominent, fresh muddy footprints. The soles displayed a distinct chevron herringbone tread pattern, leading straight toward the gurney ramp escape door at the rear of the autopsy room.\n\n\"Fuck! Someone dares to steal personal effects from the dead inside a morgue?!\" Ah-Da's terror was instantly replaced by a surge of fiery indignation, his fists clenching tight. \"That granny didn't have ten dollars on her—just a few scraps of paper and a broken tin box! Is this bastard insane from poverty or utterly devoid of conscience?!\"\n\n\"That was no ordinary thief.\" Nianzhou pulled on latex gloves, crouched down, and shone the beam over the footprints and scuff marks on the floor. \"The footprint depth is heavier on the left than the right, stride length approximately seventy-five centimeters, body weight around eighty-five kilograms. Adhering to the edges of the tread are ultra-fine yellow-brown clay and concentrated asphalt binder particles—sediment unique to the foundation mud of the unauthorized building demolition site beneath Sanchong's Chongxin Bridge.\"\n\nNianzhou dabbed a sterile swab against trace powder on the door handle and brought it to his nose: \"Also industrial-grade diesel and abraded metallic dust from high-hardness stone crushers. The intruder was the site foreman or excavator operator from that demolition site.\"\n\n\"Why would he steal that battered tin box?\" Ah-Da asked, bewildered.\n\n\"Because what was inside that tin box was not cash, but the original land deed and household registration transcript proving the elderly woman's identity and her lawful inheritance rights to that ancestral property.\" Nianzhou stood up, his voice sharp as a blade. \"To forcibly demolish old structures and claim lucrative floor area bonuses, the developer has spent the past two years driving out unyielding residents. The elderly woman had no surviving family and suffered from dementia. If she died as an 'unidentified vagrant,' her ancestral home would be bulldozed as ownerless debris, and tens of millions in urban renewal profits would flow straight into the developer's pockets.\"\n\nNianzhou turned toward the kneeling spirit of the elderly woman, his gaze softening with profound compassion: \"What that foreman didn't expect was that although she was knocked unconscious, she gritted her teeth, crawled dozens of meters, and hid the tin box deep within her padded coat until patrolling officers found her and brought her here.\"\n\nHearing this, the elderly woman's spirit trembled violently, her withered lips quivering as she transmitted a wave of memory directly into Nianzhou's mind through spiritual resonance.\n\nTwenty-five years ago, outside the Beigang Chaotian Temple in Yunlin.\n\nIt was a bustling Lantern Festival evening thick with temple incense. Her three-year-old grandson, \"Ah-Di,\" was quietly snatched away by an unfamiliar hand amidst the festive crowd, vanishing from the world without a trace. The grandmother searched frantically through every corner of Taiwan. Her husband passed away early from grief and exhaustion, so she sold the family property, slung a worn canvas bag over her shoulder, and supported herself by collecting scrap cardboard and doing odd jobs on construction sites, eventually drifting all the way to Sanchong in New Taipei, living in a ramshackle tin shack in the redevelopment zone for twenty years.\n\nEvery morning, the first thing she did was tape missing-person flyers onto utility poles; every evening before sleep, she would open that cookie tin to touch the only remaining one-month baby photo of her grandson and the two matching mother-and-child peace talismans she had prayed for at Chaotian Temple all those years ago.\n\n\"Ah-Di... Granny lost you...\" The elderly woman's wail sounded as if echoing from the bottom of a deep well, desolate enough to bring tears to anyone's eyes. \"Granny can't leave... If Granny leaves, and Ah-Di finds his way home... he won't be able to find Granny...\"\n\nStanding to the side, Ah-Da's eyes welled with tears.\n\nHe looked down at the half-charred talisman clutched in his hand, veins bulging along the back of his fist.\n\n\"Master Nianzhou,\" Ah-Da's voice was choked yet resolute, \"this case—I am seeing it through to the end. My hometown is in Beigang... When I was a kid playing in the plaza of Chaotian Temple, there was always a hunched granny sitting beneath the banyan tree by the temple gate. No matter how hard it rained or how bitter the cold wave was, she would hand cups of hot ginger tea to passing kids, showing everyone a yellowed photo and asking, 'Have you seen my Ah-Di?'...\"\n\nAh-Da looked up, tears brimming in his eyes: \"That was her! She's the 'Ginger Tea Granny' I used to see when I was little!\"\n\nNianzhou patted Ah-Da's shaking shoulder, his gaze deep: \"Since you recognized her, don't let this elderly lady remain nameless on the road to the underworld. Old Zhang happens to be patrolling nearby. Let's go take back what belongs to her.\"\n\nTwo fifteen in the morning, at the demolition site beneath Sanchong's Chongxin Bridge.\n\nCold wind and lashing rain whipped against twisted rebar and concrete rubble. A massive excavator sat idle in the center of the muddy site, behind which a corrugated metal site office glowed with the dim amber light of a tungsten bulb, accompanied by the faint sounds of counting cash and clinking metal.\n\nThe wooden door of the site office was kicked open with a booming thud by Captain Zhang.\n\nThe burly site manager, Liu Daqiang, sat at his desk holding a handheld blowtorch, attempting to melt down the pried-open cookie tin into scrap metal. Scattered across the desk were several yellowed property deeds, a household registration transcript bearing the official seal of the Beigang Township Office, and a baby photo with yellowed laminate and worn edges.\n\n\"Police! Make one move and you're in cuffs!\" Captain Zhang barked, drawing his service weapon, while two plainclothes detectives swiftly tackled the foreman as he attempted to lunge toward the window.\n\n\"Officer! It's a misunderstanding! This is scrap metal I picked out of the trash on the job site!\" Liu Daqiang bellowed, pinned against the desk as his fleshy jowls twitched frantically. \"Is picking up trash a crime?! What right do you have to arrest me?!\"\n\nChen Nianzhou stepped deliberately into the office, with Ah-Da following close behind.\n\nIgnoring Liu Daqiang's howling, Nianzhou walked up to the desk, picked up the baby photo slightly singed by the blowtorch, gently blew the ash off its surface, and turned toward Liu Daqiang.\n\n\"Scrap collectors don't break into the New Taipei Mortuary autopsy suite at one in the morning and sever public evidence lockers with hydraulic shears.\" Nianzhou retrieved a handheld UV lamp from his pocket and aimed its beam at Liu Daqiang's grease-stained palms.\n\nUnder the ultraviolet light, the tips of Liu Daqiang's fingers and his cuffs immediately flared with a blazing, unmistakable neon-green luminescence!\n\n\"The handles and locker surfaces in the forensic evidence room are routinely coated with forensic luminescent transfer powder,\" Nianzhou said, his gaze fixing coldly upon the pale-faced foreman. \"The moment bare hands touch it, the powder embeds deep within fingerprint ridges and sebaceous pores. You couldn't wash it off with soap in three days.\"\n\nStaring down at his glowing hands, Liu Daqiang's lips began to tremble uncontrollably.\n\n\"Furthermore,\" Nianzhou pointed to the steel-toed work boots on Liu Daqiang's feet, caked with yellow mud, \"the chevron tread on your soles matches the mud impressions on the autopsy room floor down to the millimeter. Even more lethal: from deep within the laceration on the back of the elderly woman's head, we retrieved heavy-duty anti-corrosion epoxy paint chips identical in composition to the bucket edge of your excavator. During last night's rainstorm, you shoved her down, watched her skull crack against the ground in the mud, and callously padlocked the site gates, leaving her to freeze to death.\"\n\nNianzhou's words landed like a verdict from the underworld: \"Intentional illegal demolition, manslaughter escalating to abandonment causing death, plus burglary of public evidence by breaking into a government office. Liu Daqiang, prepare to rot in prison for the rest of your days.\"\n\nLiu Daqiang's knees buckled, and he collapsed entirely into the muddy floor, incapable of uttering another word of defense.\n\nCaptain Zhang escorted the handcuffed suspect out of the office, while Ah-Da stepped forward in silence, gathering the scattered deeds, the household transcript, and that precious baby photo, carefully returning each one into the rusted cookie tin.\n\nOutside the site office, the drizzle had stopped, and the eastern sky began to show the pale gray tint of dawn.\n\nBeside the muddy mound of rubble, the spirit of the elderly grandmother stood quietly amidst the morning mist.\n\nAh-Da stepped forward, reverently cradling the tin box against his chest with both hands. Tears finally breached all restraint, and he sank to his knees before her phantom.\n\n\"Granny... your things have been found,\" Ah-Da choked out, his voice echoing across the silent ruins. \"The deed is back, the household registry is back... and Ah-Di's photo is safely right here.\"\n\nThe elderly woman looked down at the intact tin box. The fear and agony that had etched her face slowly dissolved into an immensely tender smile.\n\nFrom the void, accompanied by ancient hoofbeats, Ox-Head in his black trench coat and Horse-Face stepped out from the morning mist.\n\nFor once, Ox-Head held no cigarette between his lips, looking down in quiet dignity at Ah-Da and the elderly grandmother kneeling on the earth.\n\n\"Ah-Da,\" Nianzhou prompted softly, \"take out your peace talisman.\"\n\nAh-Da paused, then quickly pulled the half-charred Dajia Mazu talisman from his chest and raised it high alongside the cookie tin.\n\nThe elderly woman extended her translucent hand, stroking Ah-Da's head with a touch that was icy yet filled with the boundless warmth and comfort of a grandmother.\n\n\"Good boy... thank you...\" Her voice was no longer raspy, turning as gentle as a spring breeze. \"If Ah-Di... had grown up, he would probably be your age by now...\"\n\nSunlight broke through the cloud cover, casting golden morning rays across the grandmother's form.\n\nHer tattered floral coat and worn slippers transformed into clean, tidy blue linen robes. Her hunched spine straightened, and the age spots and weathered wrinkles melted away, revealing a kind, warm, serene countenance.\n\nOx-Head stepped forward holding an antique bronze guiding lantern, bowing slightly to her: \"Honorable elder, after twenty-five years of waiting, your earthly trials are ended. Your son and husband have prepared hot tea at the foot of the Naihe Bridge. Let us go.\"\n\n\"Uncle Ox,\" Ah-Da wiped his tears and looked up, \"what about Ah-Di? Where is the little boy she spent her whole life searching for?\"\n\nHorse-Face checked his glowing digital registry and let out a soft sigh, his voice surprisingly gentle: \"Ah-Di fell gravely ill after being abducted and passed away when he was seven. But he refused to reincarnate; he has been sitting obediently by the banks of the Naihe Bridge waiting for his grandmother... Finally, their family will be reunited.\"\n\nThe grandmother turned, bowed deeply to Nianzhou and Ah-Da, and with tears of pure peace and happiness, followed the warm lantern light, stepping lightly into the golden dawn.\n\nAs the morning mist dissipated, only a faint wisp of sandalwood fragrance lingered above the ruins.\n\nNianzhou knelt down, helped up the tear-drenched Ah-Da, and pressed a pack of tissues into his hand: \"Once you've cried enough, stand up. As a forensic doctor, let your tears fall into your heart. When your hand holds the scalpel, it must never shake.\"\n\n\"Master Nianzhou... I understand.\" Ah-Da sniffled, wiping his tears away with determination as he clutched the tin box tightly against his chest. \"I will personally suture Granny's body and send her off on her final journey.\"\n\nNianzhou looked out at the rising sun and lit the Long Life cigarette between his lips.\n\nA new day had begun, and in the forensic pathologist's notebook, yet another wandering soul had finally found her way home.\n"}];
